ur pupils dilate and somewhere bleak and broken almost comes into view at the corners of your vision."SA woman’s voice whispers from that place – almost familiar, but not quite."8You shouldn’t have reversed that amulet, dearest."<The woman who gave it to you was trying to protect you."QNow, though, charms for safe beginnings turn to invitations of dire endings."gMaybe there’s something to learn from interlacing your journey with the path of ordeals, though."zEnjoy this brief, bitter taste of the end, darling, and I’ll try and pull some strings should you prove victorious."3\i[TAROTAMULET]Once again the amulet twitches."UOnce again, you can almost make something out, just past your peripheral vision."Once again, she speaks."(Oh? You’re back, dearest. Lovely."UThese people are tied inextricably to this region’s secrets; its conspiracies."oLet me implant a bit of my demesne into theirs, and I might be able to tease them open like a faulty lock."@You want to know more, don’t you? Want them to trust you?")Then prepare to enjoy another trial.",\i[TAROTAMULET]It’s the amulet again."^It isn’t the thing itself that’s in pain. No, something else is – something larger."'Something is wrong in this region.",Another challenge, another opportunity."yI never put much stock into mysticism until my hand was forced. I’m so glad to see my investment paying dividends."MThese people don’t even know I’m threading their fate through yours!"cI paint an impressed expression on their malleable faces – so long as you can walk the walk."/Go on, dearest. You know the rules by now."R\i[TAROTAMULET]The reversed amulet spasms and the other place impends on you."-That voice… it’s painfully familiar."*Oh, you already know who I am, child."nI’m the one that’s waiting for you at the end of the line. The end of your line… and of every line."&Makya is a place rich in history."VThat’s why you endure these tastes of my demesne, isn’t it? To learn history?"=Well, even history ends. You’ll understand eventually."6Go on. Show me what a conqueror you are, darling."Z\i[TAROTAMULET]At this point, you can almost hear fate whimpering through the amulet."3Her voice shushes it, but does not comfort it."�Where did Imogene get this thing? I doubt she realized the significance of the sliver of stone she implanted within this amulet."QIt was uplifted from a forbidden place where history is tortuous and frayed."�Its latent power, the witch’s arcana, and, of course, my… expertise… all aligned to make my little bits of influence possible."-I hope you feel lucky, darling: you are."Always."\i[TAROTAMULET]....."MThere’s something calming about the hellscape you can almost perceive."*It’s a calm hell; quiet and somber." Her voice is much the same."�If only I could twist these gym leaders’ roles without having to suffuse their arenas with my demesne and all its… antipathy."*History ends quietly, but not kindly."OHere, our day-to-day lives are much like what you endure in these battles."Oh, don’t pity me. My only point is that I would gladly spare you the intensity of fate’s dying gasps if I could, trust me."Trust me, darling."v\i[TAROTAMULET]As the amulet twists and writhes, you can feel the tension of invisible threads being pulled taut."8They are wrapped around the amulet, and around you."sSomewhere behind you they frayed into thousands of strands, and ahead of you they extend to somewhere distant."There they all end.":You understand by now, don’t you? Makya is history.">You, darling, are a history to me – a singular history."3And I am a singular history projected forward."�You have the benefit of what we’ll call a privileged reference frame, and I thank you dearly for letting me glimpse through your eyes at it."0Not to mention making a few… alterations."+Don’t think too hard on it, dearest.".\i[TAROTAMULET]The amulet has gone still."^Something is changing – the threads are being woven back together, or severed, or both."4Someone is taking matters into their own hands."No, t