o you can sail on over and give it a looksie."kOh yeah, guess I didn't say before, but the Battle Monument is a big tower in the middle of the ocean."IIf I didn't know better, I'd think it was some evil villainous lair."nAnyways, I'll be hanging around the Battle Monument for the foreseeable future, so meet me here, ya hear?"JI've got some new team configurations I really wanna try against you."..."t...Ok yeah someone here just asked to battle me, and I'm not gonna turn that down, so I gotta end the call now."VHope you're doing well, be safe, make good choices, have fun, et cetera. Bye bye!"…They hung up.",They must really want to talk with you."dA couple seconds later, you receive a text message with the coordinates to the Battle Monument."Hello to you, young one."It is I, Dr. Hekata."TDo not worry about how I learned of your cellphone number. I simply divined it."2I have a topic to discuss of some importance."PI beseech you—<imp>visit my abode in Grouz</imp>. There we shall discuss."DApologies for the interruption to your adventure, young master."wHowever, given that you've sent a number of Pokemon to Storage, I thought it best that I inform you of my project."GTo make it short: Your family owns an unused Estate here in Makya."pSince you're taking on the Makyan Gym Challenge, I took the initiative to renovate the grounds for our use."dI've set up a system that sends the Pokemon you store in your PC to this <imp>PokÉstate</imp>."GI'll take care of them there while you are busy with your journey."pI love Pokemon variety, so I've prepared lots of <imp>EXP Candy</imp> to give you as your collection grows."COnce you've earned some, I'll send them to you through the PC."nI'll continue to wait for you on the boat. If you want to visit the PokÉstate, send me a ping at any PC."%I'll take you there immediately."?That is all. I will distract you no further, young master."A\i[TAROTAMULET]The Tarot Amulet spasms like something dying."uYou feel your pupils dilate and somewhere bleak and broken almost comes into view at the corners of your vision."SA woman’s voice whispers from that place – almost familiar, but not quite."8You shouldn’t have reversed that amulet, dearest."<The woman who gave it to you was trying to protect you."QNow, though, charms for safe beginnings turn to invitations of dire endings."gMaybe there’s something to learn from interlacing your journey with the path of ordeals, though."zEnjoy this brief, bitter taste of the end, darling, and I’ll try and pull some strings should you prove victorious."3\i[TAROTAMULET]Once again the amulet twitches."UOnce again, you can almost make something out, just past your peripheral vision."Once again, she speaks."(Oh? You’re back, dearest. Lovely."UThese people are tied inextricably to this region’s secrets; its conspiracies."oLet me implant a bit of my demesne into theirs, and I might be able to tease them open like a faulty lock."@You want to know more, don’t you? Want them to trust you?")Then prepare to enjoy another trial.",\i[TAROTAMULET]It’s the amulet again."^It isn’t the thing itself that’s in pain. No, something else is – something larger."'Something is wrong in this region.",Another challenge, another opportunity."yI never put much stock into mysticism until my hand was forced. I’m so glad to see my investment paying dividends."MThese people don’t even know I’m threading their fate through yours!"cI paint an impressed expression on their malleable faces – so long as you can walk the walk."/Go on, dearest. You know the rules by now."R\i[TAROTAMULET]The reversed amulet spasms and the other place impends on you."-That voice… it’s painfully familiar."*Oh, you already know who I am, child."nI’m the one that’s waiting for you at the end of the line. The end of your line… and of every line."&Makya is a place rich in history."VThat’s why you endure these tastes of my demesne, isn’t it? To learn history?"=Well, even history ends. You’ll understand eventually."6Go on. Show me what a conqueror you are, darling."Z\i[TAROTAMULET]At this point, you can almost hear fate whimpering through the amulet."3Her voice shushes it, but does not comfort it."�Where did Imogene get this thing? I doubt she realized the significance of the sliver of stone she implanted within this amulet."QIt was uplifted from a forbidden place where history is tortuous and frayed."�Its latent power, the witch’s arcana, and, of course, my… expertise… all aligned to make my little bits of influence possible."-I hope you feel lucky, darling: you are."Always."\i[TAROTAMULET]....."MThere’s something calming about the hellscape you can almost perceive."*It’s a calm hell; quiet and somber." Her voice is much the same."�If only I could twist these gym leaders’ roles without having to suffuse their arenas with my demesne and all its… antipathy."*History ends quietly, but not kindly."OHere, our day-to-day lives are much like what you endure in these battles."Oh, don’t pity me. My only point is that I would gladly spare you the intensity of fate’s dying gasps if I could, trust me."Trust me, darling."v\i[TAROTAMULET]As the amulet twists and writhes, you can feel the tension of invisible threads being pulled taut."8They are wrapped around the amulet, and around you."sSomewhere behind you they frayed into thousands of strands, and ahead of you they extend to somewhere distant."There they all end.":You understand by now, don’t you? Makya is history.">You, darling, are a history to me – a singular history."3And I am a singular history projected forward."�You have the benefit of what we’ll call a privileged reference frame, and I thank you dearly for letting me glimpse through your eyes at it."0Not to mention making a few… alterations."+Don’t think too hard on it, dearest.".\i[TAROTAMULET]The amulet has gone still."^Something is changing – the threads are being woven back together, or severed, or both."4Someone is taking matters into their own hands."No, that isn’t me."0We both know who it is, though, don’t we?"dYou should probably stop her from doing that, or one of us could end up in the other’s place."IYou were not made for the terminus, and I was not made for a utopia."=And no human was made for the paradise she’s planning.",…\PN, you know who I am, don’t you?"]We won’t be speaking for a little while, but know that I’m watching over you, child."My child."…Agonizingly familiar."[But, still, she is a stranger to you, this woman who almost has your mother’s voice."	\PN."$I’m swallowing my pride here."EI need your help with something... more important than my pride."You like that, don't you?"5Helping people? Earning some coin along the way?"iI know things are dire everywhere right now, but… that’s why I need someone of your skill level."?Someone with experience cleaning up Team Chasm's mistakes."TMeet me in the <imp>Circuit Cave</imp>, it's under the <imp>Canal Desert</imp>."…He hung up."?The last of the genies whooshed past me a few moments ago.">I poked my head out to check where they're flying off to.".East, across the ocean. I've no idea why."WShit! The Drillers spotted them too. I can see them sending out some Flying-types."DMeet me in the Sandstone Estuary, on that sandbar full of junk."Quickly!"No."Why are you down here?"Who are you?"Whose Pokémon are those?"How do you know?"I doubt it."You want it gone?"What are they good for?"I'm busy."	Why?"On my way."A few badges."Not really."Why would I tell you?"Just beat Helena."	One."Shut up."Making headway."Couldn't be better."There's been trouble."More work?"	Yep!"Not this again.Iu;␀�[[&"mPokemon Tectonic has features to help you make sense of its open world, and its many mechanical changes."rThe <imp>What Next?</imp> feature tells you what to do to progress the main story, if you forgot or got lost."7It can be found in the <imp>Game State</imp> menu."\The <imp>Battle Guide</imp> explains the battle mechanics as well as battling strategy."6It can be found in the <