issing the cash? Hmm."1You've... got your own set of problems, huh?"Formation 4C, Gurdurr!"Get ready to block 'em!"$Our defensive line collapsed...">We need to hit the gym. I hope Eko is taking challengers!"Oh… you destroyed it.">I was watching that avatar, and you just… dismissed it."&Well, it couldn’t last forever."5Nice to meet you. My name’s <imp>Skyler</imp>."OYou were superb, by the way. Fought like the sun against the morning mist."KAnd, I suppose I can’t complain. I can leave now, at the very least."Skyler."vI don’t know what else you want me to say. I’m a traveler on a pilgrimage of sorts, which I can now continue.""All thanks to you, of course."EI’d opted to take a short nap before continuing my pilgrimage."YHah. Bit of a mistake. The avatar showed up while I was sleeping, not that I minded."vMakya’s a beautiful region, full of beautiful people. But I’m going to admit that I’m here for the avatars."aEveryone’s concerned with how dangerous they are, but I think they’re missing the point."pWe’ve gotten jaded. Pokémon used to be magical. We used to worship them. I think we’ve forgotten that."%So are you! Look how you fought!"mBut I’m interested in you nonetheless. Call it a dangerous obsession or a leap of faith – your pick."[But were they always? You’ve heard legends of Pokémon raising mountains and oceans."IWe were created by Pokémon, and they’ll be the end of us someday."YAt least, that’s what they say of Arceus and Yveltal, not to mention all the rest.""I’m glad to hear you agree."pMaybe it’s a foolish endeavor, seeking these things out. I’m sure they’d maul me given half a chance."BBut maybe reverence, not fear, is what they’re looking for."LIn any case, I’m glad I met you. Technically, I suppose you saved me."LI’ll be back on my little journey now, but, uh, I’ll see you again."pA trainer like you must be seeking badges, right? So let’s meet in the <imp>town ruined by avatars</imp>."NI hear there’s a gym leader there. So long, my knight in shining armor."NMy grandpapa gave me this Tranquill. He's in the ground now. Wanna fight?"NWelp, I've gotta go! Grandpapa's gonna give me a tour of the mines today!"5Tranquill! No! Use your Tranquill powers! ...oh."Swirlix goes bye-bye..."IYou with the rangers? Ah, doesn't matter. No one's nabbing our haul!"�I swear, if our fourth was here, we'd kick your teeth in! Where'd that chick run off to, anyways? She needs some teeth-kicking too..."TI've taken worse! If you think I'm done protecting the boss, you don't know me!"7Excuse me! We were about to settle this in battle."FBut, fine, I guess we can find common ground in disposing of you."Z...Hmph. Very well. I suppose brute force is your people's specialty. Follow my lead."jBah! I have nothing left, and now she is free to waltz on in to the College. Is that what you wanted?"$No, you know what? I'm leaving."RThe only way I'm coming back is if it's with my dad and a few of his friends."KI knew who you were the second I saw your last name on the role sheet."BThe last time I heard it, it had "Lieutenant" in front of it."wIf only you'd inherited some of his prowess in battle, you might've made it past me. Go then, and don't come back."*Urgh... oh, shove off, why don't you?"You too, you old hag."eI think you'll find me back here so long as you keep trying to gain entrance, you entitled brat."uMakya's one of the few regions where creative archaeology is still legal. You're kinda lookin' like competition."oMaybe that's my cue to try a different tactic. I gotta be more subtle than challenging random strangers..."RWell ain't that a cryin' shame. Guess Makya's a bit rougher than I thought..."=Those Evolution Stones are all ours! You can't have any!"=Aagh! Fine! I'll leave! I've got my evolutions, anyways."n...I'll be back. I'll be back, and if I ever see you again, things're gonna be different. I swear I'll..." The berry plant is growing."GYo...so I heard there was like, some items to steal on this route?"0I got nothin' to say. You goo