 the fence."%Do you know anything about them?"/I heard boisterous exclamations of wonder.".It's ever so compelling, don't you agree?":Maybe they're up to something...something suspicious?"No"YesIu;␀96[[~"Hey there. Miss me?"�I finally got here – all thanks to you. I have to say, you don’t look a mite worse for wear considering how much wilderness you trekked through."FI can’t cope as well as you can – I need a hot bath and soon."KThis is the place to be if one’s looking for avatars, or so I heard."_I must have heard right, because I’ve already found more than I can count on both hands."Are you in a rush?"WAll business and no pleasure might not make you dull, but it does make you a bore."XSo come on – we’re young and free. You can take a few minutes off, can’t you?"RSkyler, at your service. We met back in the grassland, between a few avatars."BThe sun and moon were smiling on us, you came to my rescue…"AI could exaggerate further but the truth is striking enough."VBut enough about the two of us. Let’s talk about the specters roaming the town.":They’re so… arrogant. Have you ever noticed that?"�They just don’t care about us fleshy creatures – human or Pokémon. All they seem to notice is the land, each other, and a few very specific objects."II know this asking a lot, but… can I borrow a Moon Stone from you?"IThe avatars seem to notice the incredible power inside those stones."cUnless you’re asking me why a Moon Stone, in which case, well, I decided apropos of nothing."ZThat’s not entirely true – I don’t want to offend them with a clashing element."AFire, Water, Sun, the like. And Moon just fits the ambience."mSafe bet, hmm? So if you have one to spare, please let me know. I’ll pay you back with interest later."bAh, fair. I am bringing business into pleasure again, aren’t I? I’m horribly bad at this.">Well, if you change your mind, you know where to find me.">I assure you, I’ll pay you back eventually, plus extra."iWell that was quick. Honestly, you shouldn’t be so generous! Someone could take advantage of that."fI’ve never turned down someone’s hospitality, especially someone like you, but take a minute."RThink about it. I’ll make sure to pay you back, but don’t rush into this."(So, care to part with a Moon Stone?"UJust come to see me, then? I appreciate it – and I appreciate seeing you, too."aYou’ll have to teach me how you stay so composed in places like this. Sometime later, hmm?""You hand over the Moon Stone."eThank you very much. I understand these are valuable, even leaving evolution out of the picture."PIf one of your Pokémon passed up evolution for this, give them my regards."JI’ll be sure to tell you the results of this offering next we meet."fAnd repay you, of course! What do you say to dinner? There’s a place in <imp>Prizca East</imp>."iWell, you can think on it – I need to track down an avatar, and you need to beat some gym leaders."Until we meet again."CI hate to be a spoilsport, but, uh, that isn’t a Moon Stone."tI appreciate the effort, trust me – you’re very generous. I just can’t work with it, though. You keep it."-Avatars seem to care about these stones."GI want to see if I can’t make an offering. Perhaps placate them?"OAnd a Moon Stone seems the least likely to offend the ones here in Velenz."pSomething like a Fire or Sun Stone would clash, and a Leaf or Dusk Stone is more of what they already have."#I promise it’s a good cause."ZMy cousin and I like to hang out here. Take in the cool atmosphere and the night sky.":We still battle people, but like... in a chill way..."0I'm gonna leave now. Don't like your vibes."ACan you feel the energy given off by those evolution stones?"&It's doing wonders for my stress."ZIs life worth living if you can't take time to be transfixed by the beauty of nature?"SA notice about the Makyan Regional Tournament has been hastily scribbled over."6A note added below reads "Not Taking Challengers""Velenz Gym"Leader: Rafael"..."hIt seems like the Gym Leader was supposed to write a title here, but the space has been left blank."$Temporary Velenz Ranger Outpost""Velenz, proud home of-""7Claw marks on the sign render the text unreadable."=Don't tell the others, but I'm getting bored of waiting.">Well, might as well battle you before <i>they</i> arrive."BI saw a light come down from the sky and land west of Velenz."[I was hoping these stones would draw the aliens out, but it's been a week and nothing.":Since that failed, you can just take them. Good luck.")Losing? Now that's an alien feeling."TThat mansion near the menagerie must have something to do with the light I saw."TMy cousin says I'm paranoid, but I definitely saw the place glowing last night."3I thought this place was supposed to be scary."Just seems peaceful to me."$Eek! You're the scary one here!"(I'm afraid of bugs, but not ghosts."4To be honest, this town hasn't been that scary.";I'm having a good time, so I'll hang out here for now.",Got some rare things on sale, stranger!"Come back anytime."East: Repora Forest"South: Barren Crater",No earthlings allowed: that's the rule."7By the power of the Moon Stone, I will punish you!"%What? Friendship wasn't enough!?"<You're really gonna invade our special space like this?">I haven't been a real sailor since they scuttled my ship."I just like the clothes."IHey again. Bet you didn't expect to see me in a place like this, eh?"HI'm good at battling, less so at cryptic riddles and haunted towns."0But, let's not let my failures go to waste."HPut the searching on hold for now, and engage in a little sparring.":Talk to me again when you see the value in that idea."XFighting me's better than fighting any of those Avatars, I'd wager. Prove me right?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."	Boo!"%I bow to thee, oh masterful one."'Eh, that was pretty good, I guess."DSome rangers set up a rest spot in the southern part of Velenz."6Check it out, heal up your party, get back to me."2Some rangers set up a rest spot to the south."TYou unlocked Rafael's front door?! That sure saves me the time and frustration."0Much appreciated, fellow trainer! Off I go!"|Rafael may have a layer of earth protecting him from the surface, but it doesn't protect him from my astral projection."bI've been watching his battles with some fervor. I wish to grasp the essence of his strategy."'It is, at its core, about dancing."WHis Oricorio and Alolan Marowak both gain power from dancing done by their allies."JIf one was feeling particularly devilish, one could aquire a Hattrem."UThat witch has a special ability which can prevent Pokemon from utilizing dance."^There's supposed to be a gym leader around here, but he's not keen on taking challengers."6He lives <imp>underground</imp> like some hermit."8Even locked himself up to make it harder to get in."NApparently the <imp>lock combination code</imp> is somewhere in the town."JThis is all a bit too mental for me right now, so I'm taking a break."PA small handmade sign. It lists an eight-digit code in a big, blocky style."Why are you here?"Is this going somewhere?"Who are you?"	Why?"No way."
Sure."Not yet."Here you go."Why do you want it?"Maybe later."Sure, let's go.[~"嘿，想我了嗎？"�終於到地方了...再次感謝你之前幫我脫困。不過我很意外，穿過了一大片沼澤，你看起來卻並無疲憊感。"P沒想到你竟然這麼強...我不行，我得找地方洗個熱水澡。"2我聽說這裡是尋找化身的好去處。"e顯然這並不是謠言，來到這邊之後，我見到的化身已經超過兩手之數了。"你在趕時間？";如果人沒有時間娛樂，早晚有時間生病。"J盡請揮霍年輕帶來的自由吧，在這裡歇歇腳不好嗎？"V我是斯凱勒，之前在草地那邊見過，當時旁邊還有一個化身。"J當日月都對我露出微笑時，是你來救我於水火之中..."e我可以用更誇張的方式形容我們之間的相遇，不過事實就已經很夢幻了。"_關於我們的事情，差不多就聊到這裡吧，現在說說這鎮子上的幽靈。"8你注意到了嗎？它們簡直...太傲慢了。"�它們根本不在乎我們這些還擁有血肉的生物，它們似乎只在意彼此的領土，以及某些極為特殊的東西。"N我知道這個要求很過分，但我...能問你借一塊月之石嗎?"D化身們似乎注意到了進化石中蘊含的驚人力量。">至於為什麼是月之石...好吧，我隨便選的。"P倒也不是完全隨意選的...我不想用相沖的能量激怒它們。"G像是火、水、太陽那些...月亮剛好符合這個氛圍。"z這是個很安全的決策，對吧？所以如果你可以借我，那麼將來，我會連本帶利還給你的。"e啊，也對。我又把工作和私人生活搞混了，我也對自己這個問題很頭疼。">如果改變主意了，你知道到哪裡能找到我。";我向你保證，將來會連本帶利還給你的。"\嗯？這麼爽快？老實說，你不該那麼大方，很容易被別人利用的。"M我從不拒絕別人的好意，特別是你，但請先思索一下。"~思索一下是否要借給我這麼貴重的物品。當然我肯定會還給你的，但請不要隨隨便便做出決定。"5那麼，你能把一顆月之石借給我嗎？">也就是說，你是來看我的？我真的很高興。"S晚些時候，能不能教教我怎麼在這種地方保持淡定，好嗎？" 你將月之石交給他。"b真的太感謝了，我知道，即便你不需要它，它的價值也不會因此減小。"P如果你的精靈因此放棄了進化的機會，那請代我謝謝它。">再次見面時，我肯定會給你帶來好消息的。"g當然是報答你啦！請你吃頓晚飯咋樣？<imp>東宏禮市</imp>的美食挺不錯的。"k不過現在，是時候行動了...我得去追蹤一個化身，而你得打敗一些道館館主。"下次再會。";我實在不想掃你的興，可這不是月之石。"w我很感激你的心意...你真的很大方。只是這個對我來說沒什麼用，你還是自己留著吧。"/化身似乎對這些石頭很感興趣。"J我想試著能不能用這種方式，安撫一下它們的情緒？"G在夜幽市這種地方，月之石應該不會冒犯到它們。"}而火之石、日之石這些就跟這裡的氣氛相沖了，至於葉之石或暗之石...貌似它們已經有了。"&我相信自己的判斷沒錯。"D我和表弟常在這兒發呆，感受清涼夜風和星空。"8我們也會對戰，不過...主打一個佛系..."&我要走了。你氣場好怪。"/能感受到進化石散發的能量嗎？" 對緩解焦慮有奇效。"S如果連駐足感受自然之美的時間都沒有，活著還有啥意思？"S一張關於馬凱亞競技大會的通知，被潦草地塗抹後扔掉了。"7下面增加了一行註釋："不接受挑戰者""夜幽道館"館主：拉斐爾"..."Y按照慣例，館主應該在最後一行寫些什麼，但這裡被空出來了。"#夜幽市臨時護林員哨站"%"夜幽市，我驕傲的故...""5上面的字跡被爪痕破壞得難以識別。"8別告訴其他人，但我等得有點無聊了。"B算了，在<i>他們</i>來之前，不如和你打一場。"D我看到一道光從天而降，落在了維倫茲的西邊。"Y我本來指望這些石頭能引出外星人，但一週過去了，啥也沒有。"8既然失敗了，你就拿走吧。祝你好運。"/輸掉？這還真是種陌生的感覺。"D那座靠近動物園的豪宅一定和我看到的光有關。"J我表弟說我多疑，但我昨晚確實看到那地方在發光。"&我以為這地方會很可怕。")只不過是比別處安靜罷了。"$哎呀！你才是最可怕的!"#我怕蟲子，但不怕鬼。"/說真的，這裡真沒什麼嚇人的。"D我在這裡玩得挺開心的，所以我會多呆一陣子。",陌生人，我這裡有東西要賣！"隨時再來哦。"東：枯槁森林"南：荒莽火山",地球人禁止入內：這是規矩。"/以月之石的力量，我將懲罰你！"&什麼？友情還不夠嗎！？"5你真要這樣闖入我們的專屬空間嗎？"G自從他們鑿沉了我的船，我就不算真正的船員了。"#我只是喜歡這身衣服。"8又見面了。沒想到會在這兒見到我吧？"A我擅長對戰，但對解謎和鬧鬼小鎮可不在行。",不過，別讓我的失敗白費了。"2先把搜索放一放，來場小對戰吧。"5等你覺得這主意不錯時，再來找我。"Y我敢說，和我打比和那些化身打有意思多了。證明我說得對吧？"明白了。"2我會一直在這裡，直到你想對戰。"嚇一跳吧！"#向您鞠躬，哦，大師。"嗯，還不錯吧。";一些巡護員在維倫茲南部設了個休息點。";去看看，治療你的隊伍，然後回來找我。"2一些巡護員在南邊設了個休息點。"S你打開了拉斐爾家的前門？！這可省了我不少時間和麻煩。"2非常感謝，訓練師朋友！我走啦！"e拉斐爾可能覺得在地底可以安然無恙，但這並不能保護他不受我的探測。"M我一直在關注著他的戰鬥，希望自己能掌握他的精髓。"#他的對策核心是舞蹈。"Y他的花舞鳥跟阿羅拉嘎啦嘎啦，都能從同伴的舞蹈中汲取力量。"P如果一個人覺得自己特別邪惡，就能得到一個提布莉姆。"M而這種精靈有一種特殊能力，可以阻止精靈使用舞蹈。"J據說這裡有一位道館館主，但他並不喜歡接受挑戰。"=他就跟個隱士似的住在<imp>地下</imp>某處。">為了不被外人打擾，甚至把自己鎖了起來。"R而那把鎖的<imp>密碼</imp>，就在這座廢棄城市的某個地方。"P但這周圍的一切讓我有些神經過敏，我得休息一會兒了。"S一個手工製作的小牌子，其中內嵌了一個八位數的密碼鎖。"你為什麼在這？"你來這裡幹什麼？"你誰？"為什麼？"不給"行吧"還不行"給你。"為什麼要這個？"也許晚點吧。"當然，走吧。;[~"Hey there. Miss me?"�I finally got here – all thanks to you. I have to say, you don’t look a mite worse for wear considering how much wilderness you trekked through."FI can’t cope as well as you can – I need a hot bath and soon."KThis is the place to be if one’s looking for avatars, or so I heard."_I must have heard right, because I’ve already found more than I can count on both hands."Are you in a rush?"WAll business and no pleasure might not make you dull, but it does make you a bore."XSo come on – we’re young and free. You can take a few minutes off, can’t you?"RSkyler, at your service. We met back in the grassland, between a few avatars."BThe sun and moon were smiling on us, you came to my rescue…"AI could exaggerate further but the truth is striking enough."VBut enough about the two of us. Let’s talk about the specters roaming the town.":They’re so… arrogant. Have you ever noticed that?"�They just don’t care about us fleshy creatures – human or Pokémon. All they seem to notice is the land, each other, and a few very specific objects."II know this asking a lot, but… can I borrow a Moon Stone from you?"IThe avatars seem to notice the incredible power inside those stones."cUnless you’re asking me why a Moon Stone, in which case, well, I decided apropos of nothing."ZThat’s not entirely true – I don’t want to offend them with a clashing element."AFire, Water, Sun, the like. And Moon just fits the ambience."mSafe bet, hmm? So if you have one to spare, please let me know. I’ll pay you back with interest later."bAh, fair. I am bringing business into pleasure again, aren’t I? I’m horribly bad at this.">Well, if you change your mind, you know where to find me.">I assure you, I’ll pay you back eventually, plus extra."iWell that was quick. Honestly, you shouldn’t be so generous! Someone could take advantage of that."fI’ve never turned down someone’s hospitality, especially someone like you, but take a minute."RThink about it. I’ll make sure to pay you back, but don’t rush into this."(So, care to part with a Moon Stone?"UJust come to see me, then? I appreciate it – and I appreciate seeing you, too."aYou’ll have to teach me how you stay so composed in places like this. Sometime later, hmm?""You hand over the Moon Stone."eThank you very much. I understand these are valuable, even leaving evolution out of the picture."PIf one of your Pokémon passed up evolution for this, give them my regards."JI’ll be sure to tell you the results of this offering next we meet."fAnd repay you, of course! What do you say to dinner? There’s a place in <imp>Prizca East</imp>."iWell, you can think on it – I need to track down an avatar, and you need to beat some gym leaders."Until we meet again."CI hate to be a spoilsport, but, uh, that isn’t a Moon Stone."tI appreciate the effort, trust me – you’re very generous. I just can’t work with it, though. You keep it."-Avatars seem to care about these stones."GI want to see if I can’t make an offering. Perhaps placate them?"OAnd a Moon Stone seems the least likely to offend the ones here in Velenz."pSomething like a Fire or Sun Stone would clash, and a Leaf or Dusk Stone is more of what they already have."#I promise it’s a good cause."ZMy cousin and I like to hang out here. Take in the cool atmosphere and the night sky.":We still battle people, but like... in a chill way..."0I'm gonna leave now. Don't like your vibes."ACan you feel the energy given off by those evolution stones?"&It's doing wonders for my stress."ZIs life worth living if you can't take time to be transfixed by the beauty of nature?"SA notice about the Makyan Regional Tournament has been hastily scribbled over."6A note added below reads "Not Taking Challengers""Velenz Gym"Leader: Rafael"..."hIt seems like the Gym Leader was supposed to write a title here, but the space has been left blank."$Temporary Velenz Ranger Outpost""Velenz, proud home of-""7Claw marks on the sign render the text unreadable."=Don't tell the others, but I'm getting bored of waiting.">Well, might as well battle you before <i>they</i> arrive."BI saw a light come down from the sky and land west of Velenz."[I was hoping these stones would draw the aliens out, but it's been a week and nothing.":Since that failed, you can just take them. Good luck.")Losing? Now that's an alien feeling."TThat mansion near the menagerie must have something to do with the light I saw."TMy cousin says I'm paranoid, but I definitely saw the place glowing last night."3I thought this place was supposed to be scary."Just seems peaceful to me."$Eek! You're the scary one here!"(I'm afraid of bugs, but not ghosts."4To be honest, this town hasn't been that scary.";I'm having a good time, so I'll hang out here for now.",Got some rare things on sale, stranger!"Come back anytime."East: Repora Forest"South: Barren Crater",No earthlings allowed: that's the rule."7By the power of the Moon Stone, I will punish you!"%What? Friendship wasn't enough!?"<You're really gonna invade our special space like this?">I haven't been a real sailor since they scuttled my ship."I just like the clothes."IHey again. Bet you didn't expect to see me in a place like this, eh?"HI'm good at battling, less so at cryptic riddles and haunted towns."0But, let's not let my failures go to waste."HPut the searching on hold for now, and engage in a little sparring.":Talk to me again when you see the value in that idea."XFighting me's better than fighting any of those Avatars, I'd wager. Prove me right?"Understood."+I'll be here until you wish to battle."	Boo!"%I bow to thee, oh masterful one."'Eh, that was pretty good, I guess."DSome rangers set up a rest spot in the southern part of Velenz."6Check it out, heal up your party, get back to me."2Some rangers set up a rest spot to the south."TYou unlocked Rafael's front door?! That sure saves me the time and frustration."0Much appreciated, fellow trainer! Off I go!"|Rafael may have a layer of earth protecting him from the surface, but it doesn't protect him from my astral projection."bI've been watching his battles with some fervor. I wish to grasp the essence of his strategy."'It is, at its core, about dancing."WHis Oricorio and Alolan Marowak both gain power from dancing done by their allies."JIf one was feeling particularly devilish, one could aquire a Hattrem."UThat witch has a special ability which can prevent Pokemon from utilizing dance."^There's supposed to be a gym leader around here, but he's not keen on taking challengers."6He lives <imp>underground</imp> like some hermit."8Even locked himself up to make it harder to get in."NApparently the <imp>lock combination code</imp> is somewhere in the town."JThis is all a bit too mental for me right now, so I'm taking a break."PA small handmade sign. It lists an eight-digit code in a big, blocky style."Why are you here?"Is this going somewhere?"Who are you?"	Why?"No way."
