yeah, through the wringer, y’know?"*But you just gotta keep your head up."&Anyways, how about a quick match?"MPhione here hasn’t been slacking, and I want to show it a proper duel."You down?"cOh, yeah, take your time. I think I might need a few minutes to get Phione psyched up anyways."'Thanks. Don’t go easy on me, OK?"Whoa. We actually did it."GNot without some scrapes here and there – wait, let me heal you.".Figure I might as well pay you back, huh?"^Uh, kinda? I’ve trained worse, but, uh, this little fella isn’t exactly a juggernaut.">I wouldn’t be quaking in my boots if I had to face one."7OK, I think Phione’s good to go. Ready to fight?"3Good fight, good fight! Phione, you did great."OI mean, \PN, you obviously did way better, but, hey, that’s how it goes."wI used to do a lot better than this. Was pretty good, if I do say so myself, but, eh, it wasn’t really worth it."pYou ever run into someone yelling at his Pokémon after he loses and just think, like, who raised this guy?"DLike, yeah, you get results, but it’s not really sustainable."UThey have to feel like living, feeling beings first, and tools of battle second."Or, like, fifth."&You get what I’m saying, right?"fFigured as much. Look at me talking at you as if you aren’t obviously a better trainer than me."rI’m OK, but I make a lot of sloppy mistakes. Still trying to learn that whole positive reinforcement thing."LYou just gotta make them feel loved, and then they’ll try their best."RPushing them hard wrings potential out of them faster, but it burns them out."CEventually they’ll snap back, or just give up. Or leave you."iWell, sure, but they’re more than tools. They’re alive, and they have their own wants and needs."XAnd if you kinda lean into that, it works so much better than ordering them around."\Or… maybe not. Obviously you know what you’re doing. I’m not gonna preach to you."RI’ve talked enough. Probably should be listening more, but, uh, I gotta go."LMakya’s a big place, and Phione and I are gonn