e we go. I’m going to take notes this time."bI’ll admit it: I’m curious. What do you bring to the table that no other challenger does?"`No matter what praise Tamarind or the others heap upon you, don’t let it go to your head."/I’m rather more rigorous in my analyses."Let’s begin."?All of that work to get here and now you test my patience?"-Ugh. Go. I can work while you’re gone."*I reared Team Chasm from its infancy."<I turned this place from wilderness to a modern region."%I am the beating heart of Makya."HFine! One of us needs to be humbled. Show me which one of us it is."QDon’t expect this to be easy simply because I work from behind the scenes.")I made this region what it is today."]Show me what you can do – or are you just what you’ve inherited from Mavis? Show me!"SNo! I can’t – how? Eight years and I still can’t beat an arrogant child!">No, no, you and your Pokémon deserve the Patience Badge."8No, no, you and your Pokémon deserve that victory."sJust do me a favor and beat Tamarind just as badly someday. You’re not the only one with a childish rivalry."^Although – and you may know where I’m going with this – there is one other thing..."@My decision to not employ gym trainers is paying dividends."2Now there’s no one to watch me keep losing."5Your victory was unexpected, but not undeserved."/You’re not the child I thought you were."(I’m happy to give you this badge."dOh, and I would be very interested in another duel – there’s more for me to learn from you."MI’ll make the time, whenever you want to give me yours. Good day, \PN."FA screensaver image of a Luxray bounces lazily around the screen."Yo, champ in the making!"*Helena runs a tight ship around here."=Even I can't get away with just standing around all day!"oHelena understands that efficiency comes from information, and information from the flow of communication."RThat's why she's focused her gym around Electric-type and Water-type Pokemon!"=They're a strong pair in battles, sharing no weaknesses."Firstl