eats, maybe?"2Yeah, you should probably have these instead."4Nevermind, it looks like he's just like this..."Emma's Empolorium"AMy god, this park is so much better than the one at LuxTech."West: Battle Plaza"North: Prizca Castle"East: Split Peaks"You read the plaque."o"The Capital Building represents the prosperity that came after the establishment of the Makyan Congress.""i"An unbroken era of peace which followed the decades of strife, which had left much of Makya razed.""{"Makya's monarchy was unable to govern the land, and the people of Makya came together to end the region's suffering.""Kantonian-Kalosian Fusion"3Someone seems to have left a note on the sign."<"Now closed indefinitely, thanks for all the memories!""0A sign is hung on the front door. It reads:"f"We're off to Casaba Villa for the summer! Any business inquiries can be given to our assistant!"""Tata!""PBicycles are the only correct way to get around a dense town like this one."3I'm not just doing errands, right now, though."#I'm getting some circles done!"Nature's Gallery"`"Prizca has stood for over 3500 years, making it the oldest capital city on the continent.""H"The people of Prizca will prosper for as long as the city stands.""*"May it last for another 3500 years!""7"Prizca, where the future is built with the past.""1Prizca Castle predates even the city itself.";Some historians say it could be almost 4000 years old!"+The cityscape here always inspires me."=The shapes, the colors, the fashion, it's all wonderful."EIt's an artist's paradise, I can see why Noel sets up shop here."2I saw a famous singer appear out of thin air."8Right in front of that clay statue near the castle."JI tried reporting it to the rangers, but they all just laughed at me."I know what I saw!"TJust because I can't remember his name doesn't mean you shouldn't believe me..."Skeevy Eevee Pub"Prizca's East Gym"Leader: Noel"Sculptor, Battler, Artist."%I'll take your Pokémon for a --"..."BWow, you have no idea how easy it is to slip into that habit."DI'm just here to have a smoke before I have to go back to work."=The cafe inside is pretty nice, you should check it out."!Their coffee is pretty good."Bit pricey though."One-Stop Tech"@I used to be Chasm, but now I work at the Capitol Building."]Got myself a nice office and everything. A pretty decent setup for being a former grunt."uI mean, mostly everyone got off alright. Helena made sure everyone at least had a job before the Team disbanded."JI wonder what my former squadmates are doing. I hope they're alright."Noel's House"5The shops on this side of town are quite quaint.">Lot of odds and ends, stuff you won't find anywhere else!"Ironclad Dojo"$Make yourself as tough as iron!"UThe West end of Prizca was constructed rapidly over the last thirty or so years."PNo time for beauty or community to form, it's all very lifeless over there."1This side of the city is much more charming."ENoel may be chill, but the trainers in his gym are anything but."pLording their position over challengers, making them run petty errands to 'earn' the 'right' to fight them."6Makes me sick that they can be so openly corrupt."8The Houndominus has its eyes locked on its trainer."3Y'know, \PN, I never thought to ask your name."yFigured it out on the way here when I did a quick li’l background check on my client up here, and then on you too."pGuess this breaks some kinda confidentiality rule, but I ain’t never been an honorable sort: it’s Zain."KYour big brother’s hired me, lookin’ to get his reserves in shape."[Keepin’ it cool. Gotta make sure it ain’t just bravado, though. Ya know how it is."lLotsa folks talk a big talk. It’s been a while since we last had a chat, so maybe ya lost your touch."Y'Fraid not. I ain't honorable, but I do what I do, and I do a mighty fine job of it.">I got paid, I got Pokémon, and you know what that means."*Oh, ya don’t have to tell me twice."}I figure lettin’ you have a crack at 'em gives you a neat little leg up in a way