ing when you fought that guy."LYeah, yeah. Just scraped up a little. Nothing a Heal Pulse can’t fix."<Can’t tell if you’re being a sarcastic snot or not."/Doesn’t really matter. You’re welcome."/Hey, listen, this’ll only take a minute."CI just wanted to tell you… hell, is that really how I sound?":Like that edgelord? Just another self-absorbed prick?"8Heh. You’re squirrellier than a Furret sometimes."-Ah, you don’t have to tell me. I know."No sugarcoating it, huh?"Yeah. That’s fair."KYou’re being polite even now? Or are you actually telling the truth?"dListen, it really hurt admitting that you’re better than me back there. As a trainer, I mean."rBut somebody had to fight and somebody had to get Samorn out, and I’m a lot of things but I’m not stupid."XYou’ve always been better. I knew it, Mom knew it, and you… I hope you know it.">This entire competition was stupid. Mom knew you’d win."OThis was just a scheme so she could finally prove you’re better than me."…Yeah."$You know Mavis as well as I do."]I mean, yeah, makes sense. She wants an heir to the company… to the legacy… you fit."OYou know it is. Mavis is just as cutthroat as Helena – hell, maybe more."YYou think a normal mom would encourage her kids to have a showdown a continent away?"	Hah!"(It’s just that easy for you, huh?"]You’re right, of course. Just took me a lot more mulling it over to get to that point."_I’m calling this whole thing off. It’s stupid and I’m not playing that game anymore."^I’m going to collect my badges, do my best in the Championship, and then I’m leaving."PYou can tell Mavis whatever you want. She’ll offer you a job at her side."5Take it or leave it, your choice. But I’m out."%Thanks. Gonna need it, honestly."Yeah. Sure as anything."Ha. Maybe, yeah."`But I’d rather be called a yellow-bellied spoilt rich kid than Mavis’s second-favorite."MGonna be honest: don’t really care. Like I said, you do what you want."xBut, yeah, I’ve been thinking about this for a while, and that whole debacl