"\一個看起來很複雜的程序正在緩慢地繪製出看起來很科學的數據。")我可以靠給精靈喂糖謀生。" 這是個不錯的工作。"A一款名為“地獄糕點師”的遊戲全屏運行中。"_上面顯示已經累計放置了900億個油酥糕點了，真是難以置信的數字！;[
"SA complex looking program is slowly charting out very scientific looking data.".I get to feed Pokemon candy for a living."It's kind of a killer gig."=A game called "Pastry Placer" is running in full screen."AThe game has accrued over 9 septillion pastries. Impressive!0Iu;␀/[[^"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."1A Totem calls. I’ve seen more than enough."bThey got away. They won. A few that were masked, and whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."4Remember what I said about the big open secret?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them."~They’ve got at least one Regi, probably more, so there’s a strong temptation to wreak havoc. Trust me – I’d know."JHate to say it, but you just need to keep being your usual self, kid."JOr, no, I shouldn’t call you kid. Take this – you’ve earned it."AUsed to give these to Chasm strike teams, for cave scouting."UIt’ll get you just about anywhere in the region – nobody hides from you now."3So go get those badges and save the day, hero."Who are you?"Why are you doing this?"Shut up, edgelord."Who are they?"What do they want?"Why Yezera?"Not my problem."You wanted power?"You wanted money?"You wanted knowledge?"Why should I care?"Then why is Yezera..."How many Regis are stolen?"They're opening that door."Your point?[^"G葉澤拉和其他人都走了，恐怕只剩下你...和我了。"b我們贏了，我也沒有理由繼續留在這裡了，這回是真的沒什麼理由了。"J除了我即將從毀滅你和你的精靈中獲得的巨大樂趣。"A我是葉澤拉的朋友，至於我為什麼不戴面具..."G你是誰，坦白說我不關心，而且我很快就能知道。"&世界上只有那麼幾類人。"/原因自然是：羞辱你會很有趣。">如果你問的是這整件事，抱歉，無可奉告。"8人類有著強烈的洩密慾望，但我不會。" 行吧，已經談崩了。"那就開始受苦吧。"&但我不是來這裡閒聊的。"A在這裡沒人有心情講笑話，無論是我還是你。"A我知道你的實力很強，這也是你自負的原因。"A但現在，就讓我告訴你為什麼是“自負”吧。"b...好吧，那就這樣咯。看來我沒辦法讓你這油鹽不進的傢伙懂得謙卑。"G你只需要擅長玩這種簡單的過家家遊戲就可以了。"5圖騰在召喚我了，我也已經看夠了。"_他們贏了...也逃走了。包括戴著面具的人，那個傢伙，還有葉澤拉..."V我也希望知道。那個傢伙...自戀又愚蠢，我只能說出這一點。" 其他人...誰知道呢。"任何可能都有。"k但如果他們特別在意雷吉鐸拉戈，並且葉澤拉和他們在一起...甚至領導他們..."&...我想不通，這不像她。")她應該是去阻止對方的人。"`但現在，這是你的問題了，我知道你可能不太高興，\但是這是事實。";這不僅僅是一個傳說中的精靈這麼簡單。"2還記得我說的那個公開的祕密嗎？"k馬凱亞周圍的洞穴是巨人們的墓穴。我說的那些奇怪的東西，就像這個一樣。"5幾十年前，一些考古隊去研究它們。"k然後他們發現了雷吉一族、豐富的礦脈和廢墟，他們認為可以利用這些資源。"~我們得到了安德里斯和梅維斯企業的支持，於是裂隙隊應運而生，我便是最初的考古學家之一。"{...有些人想要的是...海倫娜想要屬於自己的王國，安德里斯想要成為國際犯罪組織的一份子。"D我只負責研究巨人，但有些人希望我別再插手。"t我有一支團隊和雷吉鐸拉戈的支持，但他們沒有，所以我可以研究我想研究的東西。";我有五個巨人，不需要經費，但其他人..."D如果需要實驗室設備，就會把清單發給海倫娜。"e我當時住在一個研究站裡，天天吃著泡麵...那是我一生中最美好的日子。"�我只想研究巨人，而且有了他們的幫助，就沒有人能限制我了。有時我也好奇是怎麼到那一步的。"0你讓它聽起來\如此純潔和高尚。"�我只是很好奇，才去尋求答案，我最終得到了想要的答案...又有了雷吉鐸拉戈在我身邊，還有誰能阻止我呢？"S再加上我還有強大的裂隙隊，再加上我的研究非常有價值。"J我正要說這個，但是...也許哪天能派上用場，對吧？">正如我所說：我們找到了五個巨人的塑像。"V我花了多年時間破譯它們的銘文，並理解了它們的真正本質。"Y這帶領著我們找到了雷吉奇卡斯，那時我也在加緊地進行研究。"S雷吉奇卡斯比其他巨人加在一起還要強大，而且更有智慧。"�它能夠重塑地球，將其恢復到某種初始...類似於黏土的狀態。還能創建沒有任何人能通過的封印和結界。"D我想，你也猜到了，它也可以發動猛烈的攻擊。"~它當然還可以做其他事情，比如說我們找到了一種方法，可以讓它用它的力量創造虛幻的精靈。"G但是它們即強大又凶暴，我們只能將它們關起來。"�然後當葉澤拉踹開我們的門並讓我們停止時，她的所作所為基本上證明了我們已經意識到的事情。"h我們在玩火，如果我們繼續使用雷吉奇卡斯，將有無意中毀掉世界的風險。"�起碼也是造成一些永久性的改變，所以我們把每個巨人送回它們的墓穴，然後依照規則處理好了一切。"M當然，墓穴被加固了...幾乎沒有誰能穿過那裡的防禦。"M只有其他五個巨人一起，才能打開雷吉奇卡斯的密室。"w我不知道。她對這件事的看法，與我們沒什麼不同，我們的確做過錯事，但不是瘋子。"M我也知道她的情況...並不好，但是這...這也太瘋狂了。"J誰知道呢，我們知道有些組織一直在試圖找回它們。"G但他們不可能成功。只是...葉澤拉似乎是個例外。"...可能吧。"h雷吉奇卡斯的密室在很深的地方，如果他們還沒有打破封印，那就是徒勞。"k或者他們又重新封印了它。我可以試著偵察一下，但是...不敢說能發現什麼。"Y我的意思是，如果你不幫忙，你最好習慣全是白色石頭的世界。"h如果有人徹底解放了雷吉奇卡斯的力量，那周圍的一切都會變成白色石頭。"D我不知道，我也不知道！很多事情我都不知道！"�我覺得應該去跟安德里斯，我們的護林員，海倫娜，還有其他人談談。這樣才能弄清楚情況有多糟。">如果這些小賊露面了，那就和他們打一場。"w他們起碼有一個...甚至更多巨人，這讓他們無法控制破壞的慾望，這一點我是清楚的。"P雖然我不想這麼說，但你只要保持平常就可以了，孩子。"Y或者，不...我不應該叫你孩子了。拿著這個...你一定能用好它。"/以前給裂隙隊用的洞穴探測器。"e它可以把你帶到這個地區的任何地方，現在別人對你來說都無所遁形了。"G所以繼續去拿徽章吧，然後拯救這個世界，英雄。"你是誰？"為什麼這樣做？"閉嘴吧，垃圾"他們是誰？"他們想要什麼？"為什麼是葉澤拉？"不關我事"你想要權力？"你想要錢？"你想要知識？"我為什麼要在意？"那為什麼葉澤拉..." 有多少巨人被盜了？"他們在打開那扇門"你是說？;[^"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."1A Totem calls. I’ve seen more than enough."bThey got away. They won. A few that were masked, and whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."4Remember what I said about the big open secret?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them."~They’ve got at least one Regi, probably more, so there’s a strong temptation to wreak havoc. Trust me – I’d know."JHate to say it, but you just need to keep being your usual self, kid."JOr, no, I shouldn’t call you kid. Take this – you’ve earned it."AUsed to give these to Chasm strike teams, for cave scouting."UIt’ll get you just about anywhere in the region – nobody hides from you now."3So go get those badges and save the day, hero."Who are you?"Why are you doing this?"Shut up, edgelord."Who are they?"What do they want?"Why Yezera?