 like just yesterday I arrived here in that rusty fishing boat, ready to take on the world as part of Team Chasm.",And we did! Take on the world, that is."8Not really in the way my younger self had intended."0Have you been to the Starter Store in Novo?"QIt's the only place to get your hands on those highly coveted starter 'mons."JProblem is that they require a token exchange instead of just cash..."gWish I had one of those instead of the Normal-types that fraud of a professor likes to give out..."No thanks."I'll buy.["D訓練師，我有個好消息：一筆千載難逢的交易。"E5000金錢現金。作為交換，我會給你一隻木棉球。"G你看起來像個贏家。而這......是一筆穩賺的交易！")你會後悔錯過這個機會的。")太棒了！太妙了！太絕了！"*\PN遞出了5000金錢作為交換。"A我向你保證，這是你一生中最好的購買決定！"J我很欣賞你的熱情！要是你的錢包也這麼鼓就好了！"P我向你保證，那隻木棉球是最棒的。它是精靈中的巔峰。"8如果你用它還沒贏，我只有一個建議。" 從自己身上找原因。"#真是令人懷念的地方。"�彷彿一切都還是昨天發生的 - 乘坐著那生鏽的漁船來到這裡，並作為裂隙隊的一員踏上征服世界的旅程。"5並且我們成功了！我們征服了世界！"A只是...成果...跟我年輕時的願景差別有點大。",你去過望新鎮的初始商店嗎？">那是唯一可以獲得不錯的初始精靈的地方。"/但是那兒只收代幣，不要現金..."~如果給我哪怕一枚代幣，我都不需要去那個垃圾博士那裡，領一隻爛大街貨色的一般屬性精靈..."不了，謝謝。"我買了。;["7Trainer, I bring great news: A deal of a lifetime."EFive grand in cold cash. In exchange, I'll grant you a Cottonee.";You look like a winner. And this... is a winning deal!"#You'll regret passing on this."(Magnificent! Marvelous! Magnolious!"&\PN hands over $5000 in exchange."@I assure you, this has been the best purchase of your life!"DI appreciate the enthusiasm! If only you had a wallet to match!"KI assure you, that Cottonee is the best. The peak of 'mons all around."CIf you aren't winning with it, I have but one piece of advice."Look inward."/Being back at the Fin is pretty nostalgic."{Feels like just yesterday I arrived here in that rusty fishing boat, ready to take on the world as part of Team Chasm.",And we did! Take on the world, that is."8Not really in the way my younger self had intended."0Have you been to the Starter Store in Novo?"QIt's the only place to get your hands on those highly coveted starter 'mons."JProblem is that they require a token exchange instead of just cash..."gWish I had one of those instead of the Normal-types that fraud of a professor likes to give out..."No thanks."I'll buy.Iu;␀�&[[_"Yo, champ in the making!"QSamorn might not look like it, but she was one of Team Chasm's top battlers.".Her specialties are Dragon and Bug-types."gThat makes Ice-type your silver bullet. She'll have some answers for it, but it's still a counter."qFlying and Rock are your next best bets. Steel is pretty good as well, since it resists both of her typings."7Best of luck in the final stretch of your Gym run."-Hoho! It's rare to see Samorn so lively."-Watching you two go at it was inspiring."The PC is turned off."\With how quiet the gym is, you think it'd stand out as rude if you tried to turn it on."8Among the books on history, a scrapbook stands out."&The title is "Memories of Hoenn.""<A cute sticker of a Trapinch dominates the front cover."Sorry, am I in your way?")Wait, of course I am, I'm a trainer!";I've been reading about ancient Makyan hero- trainers."*You might be even stronger than them!"3I've got to stay here and continue my studies."+Beakers of chemicals line the shelves."*The majority appear to be weak acids."KAh, \PN! I won’t waste your time by offering something hot to drink."4You’ve got a fight on your mind, don’t you?"8Good evening. Can I get you something? Tea? Coffee?"GYou’ve almost certainly wasted enough time here already, though."3Do you get nervous before facing a gym leader?"\I do – get nervous before facing a challenger, that is. I don’t want to disappoint."LI guess I shouldn’t worry. I’m called the Dreadnaught for a reason."PAre you in less of a rush than I thought? If so, feel free to stick around."I should’ve known."uExcuse me if I seem a bit terse. I’ll have to focus for this one. You’re not to be underestimated, you know."…Neither am I."BOf course. Now, if you’ll excuse me, I have to concentrate."…Let’s begin."J“Wrack and ruin broke our ships/And plucked us from our heavens.”"UOh, my apologies! It takes a short while to get my bearings again after a fight."eI get the same way when translating – which I have to assume is why that couplet came to mind.">Let me give you your badge. You’ve more than earned it."UWe don’t have to discuss it – I won’t infantilize you with obvious praise."\Speaking of plucking from heavens, though… you ought to know what that victory means."#Shall we chat a little longer?"&…Hmph. So you… ah, nevermind."[Ignore the ramblings of my battle-jumbled brain. It’s always a pleasure to duel you."…Huh. How clever."3You won, and I have a badge to present to you."[Goodbye. …Oh, excuse me. It takes me a moment to remember my manners after a battle."LCongratulations on your victory. I’d be happy to rematch you any day."TI’ve spent most of my career carefully breaking into sealed crypts and safes."=Years ago, though, I was also hired to help create them."�The wondrous abilities of the Regis made making nigh-impenetrable doors a cinch… but I’ve broken into a lot of impenetrable doors."=There is an avatar in a cave, high above where we stand."GI’d like to entrust this key to you, so that you can destroy it.".The past belongs in the past – forever."1Hello, \PN. Any good news about that avatar?"hNo? Well, then, I’m afraid I’ll have to withhold your tea and coffee privileges until there is."	Hah!"4Sorry, but I have to have some bargaining chip."!Go destroy that avatar, now."=It hides in a cave above our heads, on the mountainside."9Ah. So it’s done. I just wish we could’ve… no."(History is history. Today is today."OAnd tomorrow is tomorrow – a tomorrow without avatars, if we’re lucky."�Thank you, \PN. I think I’ll take a short break. You’re the last challenger I expected to see before the championship anyways."8You’re always welcome to stop by my home, though!"Ceremonial iron swords."'They were dated to 1800 years ago!""A fossil of an aquatic plant."dA plaque lists a very long scientific name for it. Your eyes glaze over as you try and read it."4A simple plaque simply states "Armaldo Fossil"."MThe rest of the description plate probably hasn't been manufactured yet."4The Armaldo fossil behind me was just unpacked."1I have to protect it from ruffians like you!"(Must have misjudged your character."7Unlike me, you'd never steal a priceless artifact."
Tata!",I'll be keeping my one good eye on you."4A trash can made of some sort of tropical wood."It's totally empty."4You'll have to get through me to fight grandma!"?Guess I'll go bother the scientists at the dig site again."DYou might have beaten me, but grandma's a lot stronger than me."=You must be pretty strong if you're challenging grandma."fNotes on the chalkboard describe a timeline of the Makyan monarchy, starting from 2800 years ago."3 Shieldon fossils."?One is intact, but the other two are in very poor quality.",Basic archeology techniques are listed."GThey're given in order of most to least destructive and dangerous.";The bookshelf is full of books on science and history.".They seem targeted at a younger audience."On second thought…"Let’s do this.[_"嘿，未來的冠軍！"M賽蒙可能看起來很和善，但她以前可是裂隙隊的王牌。"P她所擅長的是龍和蟲，兩種彷彿很彆扭但又很搭的屬性。"q所以最好的選擇是用冰屬性來應對，她對此有些應對措施，但仍然是一個好選擇。"�然後比較好用的是飛行屬性和岩石屬性，鋼屬性的精靈也不錯，因為可以抵抗這裡的兩種屬性攻擊。",祝你在最後的道館好運連連。"2吼吼，很少會看到賽蒙這麼活躍。"A看著你們兩個打得如此激烈，真是鼓舞人心。"電腦關著。"e道館裡面非常安靜，如果你打開它，立即就會引起注意，這十分不禮貌。"P在有關歷史的書籍當中，有一本格外引人注目的剪貼本。"&標題是《霍恩的回憶》。"2上面還有一張可愛的大顎蟻貼紙。"&對不起，我擋到你了嗎？"8等下，擋你就對了，我是個訓練師呀！"J我一直在閱讀關於古代的馬凱亞英雄訓練師的事情。"&你可能比他們還要強大！"/我必須留在這裡繼續我的學業。"/架子上擺滿了化學試劑和燒杯。"大多數是弱酸。"P啊，\PN！我不會再浪費你的時間，問你需要喝點什麼了。"2你是為了戰鬥才來這裡的，對吧？"5晚上好，需要來點什麼？茶？咖啡？"2不過，你可能不願再浪費時間了。";通常，挑戰館主之前，你會覺得緊張嗎？"_其實，我在面對你們時才會緊張，我不想給人留下一個很差的印象。"b我想我應該不用擔心，畢竟我的隊伍以前可是被稱為“銀河戰艦”啊。"8你不用趕時間嗎？那就先隨便逛逛吧。"差不多就這樣了。"n如果你還是感覺我說得偏少，只能說我一直都是如此，你是個不容小覷的對手。" ...當然，我也一樣。"J“絕望會毀滅我們的船隻，並帶領我們通向天堂。”"...開始吧。"J“絕望會毀滅我們的船隻，並帶領我們通向天堂。”"J啊，抱歉，每次打完，我都得需要一點時間來恢復。"_我在翻譯文獻是也會有這種感覺，這就是讓我聯想起這首詩的原因。"A這是我要給你的徽章，你已經完全贏得了它。"G這是顯而易見的，我不會用那些幼稚的話稱讚你。"M說道通向天堂...你應該明白這場勝利還意味著什麼吧？"我們再聊聊吧？"...嗯，你...算了"M請不要在意我戰鬥時的胡言亂語，很高興能與你對決。"...哼。",你贏了，另外還有這個徽章。"h再見...哦，抱歉，人老了之後就是這樣，打完架後我需要時間來切換心態。"J恭喜你贏得這場勝利，我隨時都願意與你再來一場。"A我的大部分時間，都在小心翼翼地保護墓穴。"G不過，多年前，我也曾被以另外的目的叫來這裡。"~巨人們的神奇能力，使我們學會了製作那種門...說是無法被攻破，其實我們自己就攻破了很多。";這座高山的山洞裡，有一個強大的化身。";我會把這個鑰匙交給你，讓你去摧毀它。"&過去應該永遠留在過去。"2你好，\PN，那個化身解決掉了嗎？"\沒有？那麼，我得暫停你喝茶和咖啡的特權，直到有好消息為止。"哈！"/抱歉，但我必須留有一些籌碼。"&現在去摧毀那個化身吧。",它就在我們頭頂上的山洞裡。"8啊，完成了。真我希望我們能夠...不。"/歷史就是歷史，今天就是今天。"V明天就是明天...如果我們幸運的話...那將是沒有化身的明天。"t謝謝你，\PN。我覺得得去休息一下，你是競技大會之前，我最不期望見到的挑戰者。",不過你隨時都可以來我家玩！"禮儀之劍。"+這是1800年前的武器！一窩Q！" 一種水生植物化石。"S一塊牌子上列出了很長的學名，瞪大了眼睛也很難讀懂它。";簡單的困擾，簡單的變化，“太古盔甲”"M下面留有一大片空白，或許準備在這裡填上詳細說明。"2我身後的太古盔甲化石剛剛才到。"8我必須保護它不會被你這樣的人玷汙！"#抱歉，是我誤判了你。"8跟我不一樣，你是一個實打實的強者。"拜拜！" 我會時刻盯著你的。",某種熱帶木材製成的垃圾桶。"裡面空空如也。";你得先過了我這一關，才能去跟奶奶打！"A我還是去挖掘現場給那些科學家們找麻煩吧。">你就算打敗了我又如何，奶奶比我強得多！"J如果你敢向奶奶發起挑戰，那肯定是有兩把刷子的。"H黑板上的內容是自2800年前開始的馬凱亞君主年表。"三塊盾甲龍化石。"A其中一塊完好無損，但另外兩塊的質量很差。"&上面是基本的考古技術。">按照破壞性與危險性，從大到小進行排列。";一個擺滿了科學和歷史相關書籍的書架。"2只是這些題材比較符合年輕讀者。"稍等..."來吧;[_"Yo, champ in the making!"QSamorn might not look like it, but she was one of Team Chasm's top battlers.".Her specialties are Dragon and Bug-types."gThat makes Ice-type your silver bullet. She'll have some answers for it, but it's still a counter."qFlying and Rock are your next best bets. Steel is pretty good as well, since it resists both of her typings."7Best of luck in the final stretch of your Gym run."-Hoho! It's rare to see Samorn so lively."-Watching you two go at it was inspiring."The PC is turned off."\With how quiet the gym is, you think it'd stand out as rude if you tried to turn it on."8Among the books on history, a scrapbook stands out."&The title is "Memories of Hoenn.""<A cute sticker of a Trapinch dominates the front cover."Sorry, am I in your way?")Wait, of course I am, I'm a trainer!";I've been reading about ancient Makyan hero- trainers."*You might be even stronger than them!"3I've got to stay here and continue my studies."+Beakers of chemicals line the shelves."*The majority appear to be weak acids."KAh, \PN! I won’t waste your time by offering something hot to drink."4You’ve got a fight on your mind, don’t you?"8Good evening. Can I get you something? Tea? Coffee?"GYou’ve almost certainly wasted enough time here already, though."3Do you get nervous before facing a gym leader?"\I do – get nervous before facing a challenger, that is. I don’t want to disappoint."LI guess I shouldn’t wo