you. The name’s Alessa."nI’m a… call me an old friend of Yezera’s. Real interested to see if you’re as good as she claims."Ya ready?"dAin’t too surprised ‘bout that one. I tried my best, honest, but I ain’t your rival. Heh."ROughta leave you to Yez. Ah, well, I figure I might get a second shot at you."1We’ll see, huh? I’ll be watchin’, kid."So y'are good, aren'tcha?"MYezera ain’t much of a liar, but I figured maybe she got a li'l rusty."bQuite a team, kid. And quite a trainer they got. I’ll be watchin', kid. I’ll be watchin'."Good day."3Did you not expect the Dreadnaught to be here?"sI’ve competed in every Championship since their inception. I wasn’t about to miss this one, avatars or no."'I want to face you. And now I can."tIt brings a smile to my face… though now that must be snuffed out, and my mind set… on the fight to come…"Z…Hmm. I lost. I don’t know why I expected to win so shortly after our last match."KAh well! It was fun while it lasted, and it was good to see you again."}In a way, I’m glad I lost so decisively. If I’d become Champion, the hassle of dealing with the gym would be a nightmare!"RGoodbye, \PN. Come talk to me again sometime, though. My door is always open."mOh, hey. I didn’t think I’d get this far. I didn’t think – well, didn’t think a lot of things."@Doesn’t matter now. Win or lose, I’m ready to face you."HAnd, uh, I’m looking forward to seeing you give 100%. Let’s go."/Yo. I’m Eifion. You’re, uh, \PN, yeah?"YThe kid who’s been running errands for Tamarind? Heard you’re, uh, pretty scary."QAbout half the trainers I talk to have lost to you at some point or another."2... I, uh, don’t plan on being one of them."
