"0A locked door. It has a slot for a keycard."'You insert the Team Chasm ID Card."#The door unlocks with a click."It's a vending machine!",However, it no longer holds any drinks.0Iu;␀M^[[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.[�"你準備好了嗎？"J即便到現在都無法阻止你...當然我也不是沒有料到。"_你接受了葉澤拉的邀請，即便這會把你帶到這個地區最淒涼的深淵。"q你認為自己是英雄嗎？還是對某些事情懷恨在心？或者只是想要面對一位前冠軍？";請不要告訴我，我更願意自己猜出答案。"e我恐怕必須告訴你，雖然葉澤拉邀請了你，但我並不會向你提供的款待。"A你們兩個可以在一個原始真理的世界裡會面。")現在，讓我窺探你的內心。"S我不會讓你再往前走一步，一個揭示騙局的世界正等著我。"8我不會允許你否認我得到啟迪的權利。"G我們開始不可避免的戰鬥吧，我等得有些厭倦了。"M人類的心靈，至少對於我的敏銳來說，是微不足道的。"\即使不考慮我的占卜，一個訓練師的靈魂也會在戰鬥中裸露出來。",向我展示你的激情吧，英雄。"8你認為我說話的方式是虛偽的標誌嗎？"e隨你便吧，你可以把我的話視為乏味或者過度，我也不再需要與你交談。"G用你最能聽懂的語言吧？恰好，我也很擅長這個。">你遲到了，小傢伙。讓女士等待很沒禮貌。";哈！我說的女士不是自己，而是葉澤拉。"\收起你這份笑意，她打扮得好的時候很好看，而且她是我的朋友。"#她應當被尊重，明白？"~現在，我有些壞消息告訴你：如果我能阻止的話，我不會讓你和她最後起舞，到這裡就結束了。"M很高興你願意聽我講話，但現在，我不會手下留情的。"8不過，因為你的禮貌，我不會打傷你。"h但你畢竟在阻撓葉澤拉，那就留下一些淤青吧。準備好了嗎？放馬過來吧。"/啊，你的臉真的很和我的胃口。"M我挺想把你帶回去見父母的，但現在我得讓你下地獄。"D哈哈！我開玩笑的，我不會再做得那麼極端了。"G但是我也不會讓你毫髮無損地離開，準備好了嗎？",你...聽著，她...別讓我分神。"P每次不得不帶她去舞會時...她穿上禮服都比我好看多了。"V總之，要把她當做女孩子看待，像對待一位女士一樣尊重她。"P啊，我不該分心想這些...別用心理戰術了，跟我好好打。"A哈！隨你怎麼說，我只不過是做個比喻罷了。"Y你想接近她，就得先過我這關，雖然老套，但這就是我的底線。"8你也可以說，我是在準備序曲，哈哈！"M說實話我挺喜歡你的，但現在得把你的幽默打出來了。"n你好，你來得...比我預期中要早一些...我正在寫一首詩，可惜永遠無法完成了。"�這黑色的拱門像是沒有星星的夜空，很快就要被華麗的雪花石膏所代替，可這卻破壞了中心的象徵意義。"A真可惜，我猜...你現在要逼我跟你決鬥了吧？"D你闖進我的領地，帶著你訓練有素的戰鬥寵物。"h我們以前就交過手了，你還反對我的美好夢想，我又怎麼有選擇的權力呢？"_不要侮辱我了。你已經做出了選擇，現在我們必須承擔相應的後果。"\好吧，至少你很誠實，我喜歡你這一點，喜歡你如此清晰的思路。"�在這個陰暗的洞穴裡，總有一束閃亮的光芒。這似乎也可以寫成詩！如果我們能有一個陷入絕望的浪漫主義者來記錄一切就好了。"J唉，我不得不將我的激情投入到分化你的團隊當中。"k當然！你在這個地區是如此傑出的一束光，你應該得到頌歌...得到十四行詩。"}另一方面，你現在站在我對面而不是和我並肩作戰，這意味著你並不像我想象中那麼特別。"M沒有信仰，真是可惜！我不想這樣做！但我必須要做。";既然我這已經是定局...那就享受一下吧。"Y什麼？你認為有詩意的靈魂很可怕嗎？虔誠的信仰讓你不安嗎？"V不被無休止的社會勞作所侵擾的真實情感讓你感到不舒服了？"Y好吧，享受那種狹隘的看法吧。也就是說：你將在這裡輸給我。"你好，朋友。"J我們已經開始行動了，雷吉奇卡斯將很快重塑世界。"S我知道你來這裡是為了見葉澤拉的，但很抱歉我不能允許。"�你成功的概率接近於零，但我不是賭徒，不會選擇放任。如果你願意，我們可以一起待在這裡，直到逆轉影響到我們。"b我也是這麼覺得的。不好意思，但在現在這種情況，我必須和你戰鬥。"k真正的知識正在接近，我想在那裡見證它...如果可能的話，我也想獨自一人。"b我也不想，不幸的是，我可以從你的語氣中感覺到我們確實將要決鬥。"Y我不願讓你繼續前進，也不願輸給你。請理解...並考慮認輸吧。"D如果你要直面葉澤拉，這已經是保守的估計了。"b只要她想，她就是無敵的，儘管我也聽說了，你已經多次打破了慣例。"P現在，我們可以結束理論討論，再引入另一部分數據嗎？"J請原諒我囉嗦，如果你想直接進行決鬥，那就來吧。"V我不會侮辱你的智慧，假裝我們不會打架，那沒有什麼意義。"開始吧？"&哦...嗯...我直奔主題了。"G你曾經打敗過我，也打敗了葉澤拉，嗯...很多次。"k雖然其中一些場次，因為她用了別人的隊伍，或者其他什麼原因而不能算數。"_但問題是，我打不過你，也還是...必須嘗試。我有很多問題要解決。"Y我必須去彌補自己曾經的過錯，你就不能讓我得到這個機會嗎？"G沒錯，我知道是這個答案，你什麼都不會讓給我。"Y我本來那麼努力，就要成為冠軍的！但是...沒錯，一切都玩了！"S你很多方面都超過我了，我打不過你，但我會用其他方式！"w對你來說可能是這樣，但對它們來說不是...不是對精靈來說，是那些必須原諒我的人。"n是時候讓他們不再接受命令，被平等對待了。這也包括像你這樣的頂尖訓練師。"h我知道你不能容忍這一點，所以...我想我們得打一架，抱歉...但我不後悔。"&大多數時候我不會這樣。"t我正在盡我最大的努力去改正曾經的錯誤，你敢說這樣的話嗎？你只是在維持現狀。"k這是你想要的世界嗎？你是個富家子弟，所以...沒錯，沒有壓力，生活美好。"M哼，如果可以的話，我會讓你的生活變得更艱難一些。"2抱歉，或許我就是個惡毒的混蛋。"e不！我會失敗的...我很樂意失敗...但我不會放棄。我有需要保護的朋友。"D我有需要去彌補的過去，有需要去建設的世界。"{一個更好的世界...一個更加平等、公正的世界。對，這不是你想要的，但我不會因此而屈服。"準備好了嗎？")...嘿。這在這裡了，對吧？"S你不會...大概...改變主意對嗎？忽略了正義、公平和懲罰？"h呵，是我看走眼了...你就是塔瑪琳的走狗，大概...從一開始就在為她做事！"J你知道這意味著什麼嗎？沒錯：是時候付出代價了！"~沒錯，他們也這麼說，你不是這個團隊的普通士兵，你...大概...是個...暫時失去權勢的策劃者！"e呵，你們都一樣，我已經幹掉了很多士兵了，這次也不會有有什麼例外！")不，我真的真的很想打你！"\既然我打不到塔瑪琳，那你就是最好的選擇，過來讓我揍你一頓。";如果你真的抱歉，就別再繼續了，白痴！"q你真是個...蠢貨！我怎麼才能讓你明白你是壞人？我能把這些打進你的腦袋裡嗎？"q如果必須的話，我會捲起袖子親自揍你！如果弄壞了我的指甲，我甚至會殺了你！"8來吧，我的同伴們！我們要打敗他們！"啊。哈，哈哈哈！"�就這樣吧！預言已經完成了...這場戰鬥在這裡留下的，這些古老石頭上的傷痕，就是未來的預兆。"J你能猜到它說了什麼嗎？它說我會失敗，你會獲勝。",哈！命運似乎有一種幽默感。"S繼續吧，去更深處。我知道我的位置，不會再違抗命運了。"V為了我的理智，我將不再嘗試預測你未來戰鬥的結果。告辭。"哦，你不該這樣。"_你對我全力以赴了？我覺得連一半都沒有，你完全就是在享受戰鬥。"�繼續吧，葉澤拉在等你，我對計劃是否成功並不在意，無論結局如何，葉澤拉都會變成一個勇敢的女孩。"_一定...比我更堅強，所以你去做你計劃中的事情吧，無論那是什麼。"t還有如果你敢傷害她，屍體永遠都不會被找到，吧啦吧啦吧啦，你知道我要說什麼。",祝你好運吧，之後再來找我。";...走吧，現在就走吧。在我發火之前走。"D宇宙的命運真的取決於我們訓練精靈的技能嗎？"h這太荒謬了！太愚蠢了！我簡直不敢相信...走！走！我應該...我應該...走！"z我知道了，請原諒我...我根本沒有提供足夠的力量，我發現自己沒有任何挑戰你的手段。"S...明白了，我別無選擇，只能撤退，祝你接下來厄運纏身。"A如果你允許我離開，我不會再阻礙你的進展。"&再見...還是別再見的好。"該死！該死！"D我...對，就是這樣。我從來不像你們那樣厲害。"b我努力訓練我的精靈，試圖達到那個水平，現在...試圖彌補所有過錯。"M對不起，大家。對不起，瑪納霏。我想那就是結局了。"\讓我們把你們送回精靈中心，好嗎？讓你們恢復過來...我很抱歉..."8呃！我...沒事！哎，我想我捱了一槍..."t看著我的眼睛，你這個愚蠢的傢伙！如果我不是...呃...如果我不是...我...有點頭暈..."V這就是他們輸掉之後...會暈倒的原因嗎？我...我要...我不行..."A你這個榆木腦袋...去做...大概...你想做的吧..."h但你畢竟在阻撓葉澤拉，那就留下一些淤青吧。準備好了嗎？放馬過來吧。"Y你想接近她，就得先過我這關，雖然老套，但這就是我的底線。"&我早就該想到她沒用了。"b葉澤拉就差一點，就差一點，如果她沒有告訴你，那就能得到一切了。"�她就不該是人類，她唯一的可取之處，就是她身上非人性的成分。現在她背叛了它，也背叛了我。"8外表上或許吧，但實際上有夠噁心的。"b和其他人一樣，只有膚淺、愚蠢的慾望，我想我和她一樣都是個白痴。")對對對，很好。為她高興。"e但這無論是對她的，還是我的計劃都不是好事，希望這種宣洩是值得的。"D是的，她做到了，我很高興你能意識到這一點。"/好吧，希望永遠不會再見到你。"2但是，結束之後，我會照顧她的。">但你，我現在就得處理掉，就這樣再見吧。"G想讓我再處理你一次嗎？來吧，想多少次都可以。"不！")我需要它！我非常需要它！"5我會...你不明白，你什麼都不明白。",你們這些生物讓我感到噁心。"5好吧，你贏了。去和葉澤拉會合吧。"2我希望她能讓你明白自己的位置。";如果再見面，對我們誰來說都不會好過。"我要走了。"不。"是的。"你要阻止我？"讓開"你覺得你能？"閉嘴吧"那好吧"我不想這樣"打扮好的？"能否起舞由我決定"我沒有強迫你"對，來吧"給我的詩？"還是很噁心"不可能"我不想打架"接近於零？"說夠了吧"不行"這是錯的"不要自怨自艾"放棄吧"我不是她的手下"必須這樣做？"對不起"那就來吧"她是人類"她做得很好"她做到了" 閉嘴，是時候算賬了;[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time.00Iu;␀-[[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization. All-encompassing. And we had to be: lots of work to do."uOver just a few decades, we imposed law on this place, created entire new settlements, made it rich and vibrant."�We quintupled the population. We dealt with outbreaks, infighting, earthquakes. We secured the support of multiple major companies."~And at the end of the day, we managed to go legit, integrate with the Prizcan government, and aren’t even hated for it."_If you want to try and do even a tenth of that without resorting to violence, be my guest."�We punished people, which you’d call assault. We imprisoned them, which you’d call kidnapping. We taxed them, which you’d call theft."FOh, sure, people resisted us, but we only acted how a state does."ECandy’s too young to have been around during Chasm’s zenith."~She’s got a child’s notion of justice, and she thinks that performing her own little acts of violence fixes anything."GMaybe she should ask herself why almost everyone’s fine with us."	Yes."Andris did it for money."Helena did it for power."WAnd I did it so I could finally have the resources to properly research the Regis."ZEveryone in Team Chasm – in any organization – has their own reasons to be there."F...We can argue all day, kid. You’re not going to get anywhere."Let me put it this way:"�a lot of the Pokémon Candy has “rescued” were given to Chasm grunts for combat purposes, but they ended up liking their new home plenty fine."PMaybe talking things out would’ve resolved things better than theft, huh?"gBut I know you want to know. What’s up with Velenz? Well, it’s simple. We were trying to work."�I can’t work when I’m being attacked by wannabe heroes. When the power grid is being fried. When Ghost-types are being sent to haunt my lab.";We asked, repeatedly, for them to stop. They didn’t."tSo I took Regigigas and had it carve up the bedrock around here, then dragged some avatars in for good measure."zThey couldn’t prove it was us, but pretty soon they lost their base of operations, and that got the message across."LYes. Was. If they’d wanted to keep it, they could’ve left us alone."?Kid, have you ever gotten twelve hours of sleep in a week?"vThese “freedom fighters” were using every trick in the book. Constantly harrying us. Never a moment’s rest.".Ugh. Makes me mad just thinking about it."I think so, yeah."NThat’s how it goes. Warfare ain’t pretty, but it exists for a reason."qI did what I did. And if someone wants to “bring me to justice” for it, I say: what does that even mean?"LI’m breaking my back running this region, making it better every day."fYou want to throw me in prison? Make this place worse so you can have your petty revenge? Idiocy."SI know what I did, and I’m not going to do it again. Neither is anyone else."|...Now, kid. I need to get out of this place, because I don’t particularly want to run into Candy. Get out of my way."NYou need to work on your active listening. I didn’t ask you a question."MI told you what you were going to do… and now you’re going to do it."Ugh. Heroes!"3Damn heroes... well, what’d I really expect."Get up."CI’m not angry, just disappointed. But I will be taking my–"\PN! Tamarind!"xStop right there. I – I know I took, um, a little bit to get here, but that’s only because I was eavesdropping!";Candy, is it? Good to meet you in person... I suppose."5You know where I stand. And I know where you do."�I’ve just settled things with \PN, so why don’t we have a chat in private? \PN, be a dear for me and leave us. I’d like to end this grudge here and now."Z...Alright. This is between you and me, anyways. \PN, you can go, like, wait outside."+Just for a minute. This’ll be quick.".Good. Glad we can see eye to eye on this."You first."Not my idea."Getting answers."Delivering justice."Tyrant."You seized power."And Velenz?"You don't rule anymore."Not just violence."Some hate you."You did it for yourself."It was their home."That seems excessive."Fair enough."..."No."...Alright.[]"\PN。"J我一開始就覺得這是個陷阱，但沒想到你會在這裡。"/嗯...能解釋一下你在做什麼嗎？"4什麼？我解釋這個？夜幽市？*聳肩*"G嗯，我能猜到，但現在你是站在我面前的那個人。"_笑話。永遠不要把英雄主義帶到現實中，英雄總是會給大家添麻煩。";*哼* 隨便吧，孩子，你說什麼就是什麼。"e我知道你和那個...叫糖兒的女孩在這裡。海倫娜已經注意她很長時間了。"M不過，她並未造成太多麻煩，所以我們也就沒太在意。"k聽著，我們統治著這個地區，你應該明白這意味著什麼...你最學過政治學嗎？"J政治就是需要一些暴力手段，每個政府都是一樣的。"5你可以管我叫暴君，但我不是小偷。",而且還是一個非常出色的人。"_但也不是絕對的...安德里斯和海倫娜組成了這個地區的另外兩個角。"P更別說裂隙隊最鼎盛時期，那龐大且複雜的官僚系統了。"e從誰那裡奪走的？在我們來這裡之前，馬凱亞更是一個無法無天的地區。"V除了最初望新鎮的那群頑固分子，其他人都不抵觸融入我們。"n成為暴君的好處是什麼？如果有人故意與你做對，你可以“說服”他們停下來。",呵，本以為你的家教會更好。"J我們仍然統治著這個地區，因為我們就是這個地區。"�這裡的每一處土地上都有我們的老兵，只要一聲令下，他們便會服從。海倫娜也有她自己的追隨者，因此我們有了龐大的情報網絡。"n是她在光華市現在的位置創造了那座城市的一切，並依靠科技發展我們的經濟。"e我們是一個龐大的組織，無所不包，無所不有，因為我們必須得這樣做。"�我們用了僅僅幾十年的時間，便在這裡頒佈了法律，創建了人類的聚落，使其變得富有且充滿活力。"�這個過程中，馬凱亞的人口增長了五倍，我們處理了疾病、自然災害，還有一次又一次的內部紛爭，並獲得了多家大公司的支持。"~並最終得以與宏禮市的政府融合，在將混亂控制在最小的情況下，讓一切平穩過渡到現在這樣。"h如果你覺得想要達成這個目標，一點暴力都不需要使用，那就自己試試吧。"{我們對罪犯的懲罰被視為攻擊，我們對他們的監禁被視為綁架，我們對他們徵稅被視為盜竊。"J當然，有不少人反對過，但是國家的發展更加重要。"J糖兒她畢竟年紀小，沒有經歷過裂隙隊的鼎盛時期。"V她對正義的概念像個孩子，認為自己的小暴力可以解決問題。"\我覺得她應該問問自己，為什麼幾乎其他所有人都對我們很滿意。"沒錯。" 安德里斯是為了錢。"#海蓮娜是為了權力慾。"A我這麼做是為了能有足夠的經費來研究巨人。"_裂隙隊裡的每個人...不管在哪個組織中，他們都有自己的利益訴求。"\...孩子，就這個問題，我們可以爭論一整天，但不會有任何進展。"這麼說吧："{糖兒所“拯救”的那些精靈，的確是因戰鬥目的而徵收的，但它們也漸漸喜歡上了新的生活。"q你覺得它們真的想回到原主人身邊嗎？就算是，那談判也比偷竊更容易解決問題。"A我知道你最關心的，還是夜幽市的情況對吧？"�很簡單，我們在正常工作的時候，被一些自稱為英雄的人攻擊了，他們燒燬了電網，並派出幽靈精靈去騷擾實驗室。"P我們一次又一次地，要求他們停下來，但顯然沒什麼用。"t所以我只能帶著雷吉奇卡斯，去那裡打通地下隧道，並創造出一些化身來保護設施。"}在我們反攻之後，他們很快就丟盔棄甲了，如今夜幽市的樣子就是這一場騷亂的直接結果。"e是的，過去是的。不過如果他們想保住它，只要不來打擾我們就可以了。"4你有過一週只睡12個小時的經歷嗎？"�這些所謂的“自由戰士”幾乎把你能想到的詭計都用了一遍。在不斷地騷擾下，我們很多人每天只能睡一兩個小時。"啊...想想就來氣。"我就說吧。"G事實就是，戰爭並不美好，但它存在是有原因的。"}我只是做了自己該做的事，如果有人想要因此“將我繩之以法”，那我只想說：那又怎樣？"D我正在努力經營這個地區，讓它每天變得更好。"q你要把我送進監獄嗎？這隻會讓這個地方變得更糟，唯獨滿足了你小小的報復心。"k我很清楚以前做過些什麼，但之後不會，也不需要再做了，當然其他人一樣。"Y現在，孩子，我該離開這個地方了，因為我不想碰巧遇到糖兒。"J你需要改善你的思維方式，而且我並不是在詢問你。"5我只是告訴你，你現在需要這樣做。"呃...英雄？">去特麼的英雄...好吧，我到底在期望什麼？"起來。">我沒有生氣，只是失望。但我會帶走我的..."\P