ROFL."?The insurance business is all about predicting the future."*Too bad I'm completely unpredictable!",Well, I definitely didn't predict that."<Excuse me, I've got to update my mathematical models..."GNo matter. Even a loss is just more data to feed to the algorithm.".Crunching numbers like Sharpedo, oh yeah."%I'm just here for business, kid."#Doing a run for a few friends."_I'm wondering what made those strange grassy holes in the Amber Hills and the Floral Maze."0There's another one out by the Fin as well."QI ain't one of those superstitious types, but they don't look natural to me."&This place's got some sick stuff.";Sometimes, the hacker lady gives me rips of old games.".The publisher isn't gonna like that, heh."No"YesIu;␀�[[1"KAn old, beaten up laptop. A couple dozen windows are open all at once."RSomething is being researched, but it's impossible to tell what specifically."QIt's Nora's laptop. She must have forgotten it in her hurry to get to Svait."XA map displayed on the screen shows a path to the west of the Ranger Station there."q“Over 2500 years ago, there existed a sect of itinerant priests who worshipped a Legendary Carver of Clay."^And by its hand, people were able to claim dominion over inhospitable lands high and low."sYet, despite their efforts, humanity was cast out from the lands where the primal forces of this world worked."gBack to the caves; which their species used to call home. Now the caverns would be their tombs…""sGuess I forgot to keep the door locked… but I can’t really turn away the esteemed Champion \PN, now can I?"sI don’t know why you’re here but, if I had to make a guess… you’re searching for something; like I am."GName’s Nora. I like to think of myself as a seeker of knowledge."mI took up a job as a janitor here to gain access to this library, since it’s sealed off to the public."?It’s not trespassing if they’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records they’ve shoved away here."_Translated passages with way too many sticky notes go over all kinds of myths and legends."\One that caught my eye involves the Seekers, those ancient priests I mentioned earlier."tThey were ultimately destroyed by a great darkness that some protector deity was apparently equipped to handle."dBut, based on the fact that the Seekers disappeared, the guardian must have failed in its duty."Why? I don’t know."ZThe notes here make reference to materials that I can’t find anywhere in this room."?I’m thinking that these records have to exist elsewhere."�And I’m going to assume that they must have been saved digitally, as there’s nowhere else in the region with this much literature."mDo you think you can search LuxTech for any servers hosting data from before Team Chasm was established?"VI’ll keep on searching here in the meantime for something hidden in the stacks."7Let me know if you find something over at LuxTech."PI’ve only been finding fun facts, the kind you’d see on a moving truck."IDid you know that hexagons were an important symbols of the Seekers?";That’s apparently what inspired Team Chasm’s logo."You’re back! Excellent.":I managed to make a breakthrough while you were away."9Would you mind showing me what you’ve found first?"%You hand over the Old USB Drive.")Nora loads the device on her laptop."Fascinating."�This one file, Project Chrysopoeia Albedo, goes into great detail of a large volcanic eruption thousands of years ago which heavily impacted the region."uIt makes sense that the large clouds of ash would be devastating to a civilization in its technological infancy."BThis must be the "great darkness" that the Seekers mentioned."qPerhaps that’s also why they built what would become the underground ruins; like those found in Mt. Kilna?"CMaybe those places were meant to be safe spaces from the smog?"KWait, no. Why would they have built shelters if they had the guardian?"2Hahaha. This is the rush I’ve been seeking."0Questions whose answers are more questions."tAs for my own findings: I found references to an aboveground ruins site which might lead to what we’re after."GI’ll be waiting for you in <imp>Svait, on the upper level</imp>.[1"M一臺破舊的筆記本電腦，同時有幾十個窗口被打開了。"D有些還在研究中的內容，但看不懂具體是什麼。"Y這是諾拉的筆記本電腦，她肯定是急著去霜皚鎮，忘了帶上它。"M屏幕上顯示的地圖上，有一條從霜皚鎮往西走的小路。"`“2500年前，有一個巡迴祭祀教派，一直崇拜著傳說中的粘土雕刻師。"Y在它的幫助下，人們才得以在高低崎嶇的荒涼土地上繁衍生息。"q儘管他們付出了許多努力，但人類終究還是被世界上最為原始的力量趕出了那裡。"T洞穴，那是它們曾經的家園，洞穴，那將成為它們的墳墓...""_哦？看來我忘了鎖門了...不過我也不能拒絕尊貴的冠軍，\PN，對吧？"k我不知道你為什麼來這裡，但根據我的猜測...你應該像我一樣，在找什麼吧？"M我是諾拉，我一般喜歡將自己稱為“知識的探求者”。"n為了能進入這座圖書館，我特意應聘了這裡的管理員，畢竟這兒並不對外開放。"M現在我有正經理由待在這裡，就不能算是非法入侵了。"h從他們藏在這裡的記錄來看，裂隙隊顯然也是從人類學開始一點點入手的。"h這些經過翻譯的文獻上，大大小小的全是便籤，其中涉及到各種神話傳說。"V我最在意的還是那些探索者...當然也可以管他們叫古代祭司。"}他們最終被龐大的黑暗能量毀滅，而他們所信仰的守護神，顯然沒有應對這種黑暗的方法。"Y那些探索者就此銷聲匿跡，而這位失職的守護神也不見了蹤影。",至於具體的原因，我不知道。"J這裡的註釋當中提到了這個圖書館沒有收錄的材料。"5或許這些記錄存在於其他什麼地方。"z考慮到裂隙隊，這些文獻有可能是以數字形式保存下來的，不然我想不到它還會在哪兒。"z你能在光華市的檔案中，搜索到一些裂隙隊解散之前，所存放的數據或者服務器地址嗎？"P當然，我也會試著在這裡，找找有沒有其他相關的內容。"G如果你在光華市找到些什麼的話，就來告訴我吧。"P我這裡只看到一些趣聞，類似在搬家卡車上那種小故事。";據說那些探索者的標誌，是一種六邊形。"/恐怕這也是裂隙隊標誌的來源。" 你回來了！太好了！"D在你去那邊蒐集材料時，我這裡也取得了突破。"/能先給我看看你找到了什麼嗎？"你將舊U盤交給她。",諾拉將其鏈接在筆記本上了。"太驚人了。"�這份名為“瑩潤金成計劃”的文件裡，詳細描述了數千年前的一次規模浩大的火山爆發，以及其對該地區造成的嚴重影響。"_大量的火山灰對於正處於技術萌芽階段的文明造成了毀滅性的打擊。",這一定就是“龐大的黑暗”。"\或許這就是他們建造地下城市的原因？就像基爾納山發現的那些。"G或許這些地方本就是躲避火山灰影響的安全地帶？";等等，不對勁！他們不是還有守護者嗎？",哈哈哈，這就是我所追尋的！">問題接著答案，答案又會催生出新的問題。"}對了，還有我這邊的發現：我找到一個地面廢墟的參考資料，那裡或許有我們要找的東西。"P我會到 <imp>霜皚鎮上層</imp>，海拔稍微高點的地方等你。;[1"KAn old, beaten up laptop. A couple dozen windows are open all at once."RSomething is being researched, but it's impossible to tell what specifically."QIt's Nora's laptop. She must have forgotten it in her hurry to get to Svait."XA map displayed on the screen shows a path to the west of the Ranger Station there."q“Over 2500 years ago, there existed a sect of itinerant priests who worshipped a Legendary Carver of Clay."^And by its hand, people were able to claim dominion over inhospitable lands high and low."sYet, despite their efforts, humanity was cast out from the lands where the primal forces of this world worked."gBack to the caves; which their species used to call home. Now the caverns would be their tombs…""sGuess I forgot to keep the door locked… but I can’t really turn away the esteemed Champion \PN, now can I?"sI don’t know why you’re here but, if I had to make a guess… you’re searching for something; like I am."GName’s Nora. I like to think of myself as a seeker of knowledge."mI took up a job as a janitor here to gain access to this library, since it’s sealed off to the public."?It’s not trespassing if they’re paying you to be here."jTeam Chasm apparently had roots in anthropology, based on all the records they’ve shoved away here."_Translated passages with way too many sticky notes go over all kinds of myths and legends."\One that caught my eye involves the Seekers, those ancient priests I mentioned earlier."tThey were ultimately destroyed by a great darkness that some protector deity was apparently equipped to handle."dBut, based on the fact that the Seekers disappeared, the guardian must have failed in its duty."Why? I don’t know."ZThe notes here make reference to materials that I can’t find anywhere in this room."?I’m thinking that these records have to exist elsewhere."�And I’m going to assume that they must have been saved digitally, as there’s nowhere else in the region with this much literature."mDo you think you can search LuxTech for any servers hosting data from before Team Chasm was established?"VI’ll keep on searching here in the meantime for something hidden in the stacks."7Let me know if you find something over at LuxTech."PI’ve only been finding fun facts, the kind you’d see on a moving truck."IDid you know that hexagons were an important symbols of the Seekers?";That’s apparently what inspired Team Chasm’s logo."You’re back! Excellent.":I managed to make a breakthrough while you were away."9Would you mind showing me what you’ve found first?"%You hand over the Old USB Drive.")Nora loads the device on her laptop."Fascinating."�This one file, Project Chrysopoeia Albedo, goes into great detail of a large volcanic eruption thousands of years ago which heavily impacted the region."uIt makes sense that the large clouds of ash would be devastating to a civilization in its technological infancy."BThis must be the "great darkness" that the Seekers mentioned."qPerhaps that’s also why they built what would become the underground ruins; like those found in Mt. Kilna?"CMaybe those places were meant to be safe spaces from the smog?"KWait, no. Why would they have built shelters if they had the guardian?"2Hahaha. This is the rush I’ve been seeking."0Questions whose answers are more questions."tAs for my own findings: I found references to an aboveground ruins site which might lead to what we’re after."GI’ll be waiting for you in <imp>Svait, on the upper level</imp>.Iu;␀�[[/";Wow! It's a Volcanion, trapped inside a large boulder!"(Hey, \PN! Come around to the front."~It’s still so striking to me that at any time, Team Chasm could’ve added this protector of the region to its arsenal."oSure, they managed to capture Heatran, the Titans, and other oddities I still need to comb that USB about."cBut were they so dominated by Yezera that they thought Volcanion wouldn’t make a difference?"eIt makes me realize how terrifying going against a single person with overwhelming power can be."...as you showed me, \PN."Anyway, ready?">Nora brings out a small MP3 player, and presses a button."<A soothing recording of an ancient flute fills the air."IAh. Seems like we have unwanted guests at this once private concert."6Awesome. At least they look in the mood to dance."SI guess we can crack some heads open, show them a genuine mosh pit experience."What do you think, \PN?"qAh. I realize now that, while I patched your team up after our battle, I’m out of supplies to heal my own."I’ll be counting on you!"What a painful cry…"�I can’t imagine how it must feel to wake up thousands of years after the disappearance of the people you were meant to protect."QI realize now that I’ve only thought about how others would USE Volcanion."6As a tool, a reward, or something in that vein…";I haven't been seeing this creature as a living being."!I saw it as words on a page."7Volcanion seems to be looking to you for guidance."Take Volcanion with you?"ENora, seeing your intent, comes over and hands you a Poké Ball."AThe Volcanion seems to sigh in relief as it enters the ball."Wonderful.">Well, I guess this is where we go our separate ways, \PN."JI hope you don’t mind, but I’m going to keep the USB you gave me."{Turning away from it all now would be to live a life knowing what passion is, but never permitting myself to experience it."{There are other loose ends left behind by Team Chasm, the Seekers, and who knows what else that I want to see through."Toodles."*Volcanion nods. It will wait for you."II still think it’d be for the best if you took Volcanion with you."DI’ve spent so much time looking towards the past for answers."BThough, I guess I can keep them company for the time being…">The snow here seems to be heating up directly into steam."IIs this what Svait looked like before Team Chasm did what it did…?"aThe sublimation seems to be a different effect from the subthermal vents in the Svait Sauna.">But maybe… The sources of those phenomena are the same?"Yes"No[/">哇，是一隻被困在石頭裡面的波爾凱尼恩！"嘿，\PN！來這邊！"q按照裂隙隊的行事風格，他們總會把所有能利用的力量都變成自己的武器，可是..."Z就像席多藍恩和巨人們那樣，我還得繼續梳理一下U盤裡的內容。"e還是說因為葉澤拉的控制，才導致他們對波爾凱尼恩的態度發生了變化？"_這讓我意識到，與一個擁有壓倒性力量的人為敵是多麼可怕的事情。"#就像你對我來說，\PN。" 總之，準備好了嗎？"G諾拉拿出了一個小型MP3，並按下了其中一個按鈕。"&舒緩悠揚的古笛聲響起。"D啊，看來有不速之客闖進我們的私人音樂會了。"G也不錯，至少它們看起來，也有共舞一曲的心情。"\不過我們還是把它們的腦袋敲開，展示一下什麼叫“大場面”吧。"你覺得呢，\PN？"w啊，有點糟糕，我之前在戰鬥後為你的精靈恢復狀態，結果導致我自身的藥品不夠了。" 看來只能指望你了！" 這哭聲...痛徹心扉。"_我永遠無法想象，這種在本應保護的人離開數千年後才醒來的痛苦。"Y我現在才意識到自己之前只顧考慮別人如何利用波爾凱尼恩了。",將其作為工具、武器、獎勵..."&它是一個活生生的個體。")我卻把它看作是一頁文字。"2波爾凱尼恩似乎在等待你的指示。"#要帶走波爾凱尼恩嗎？"G諾拉看出了你的意圖，走過來遞給你一個精靈球。"J波爾凱尼恩似乎在進入精靈球的一瞬間鬆了一口氣。"太好了。"8好吧，也到我們說再見的時候了，\PN。"9但我會留下這個U盤，希望你不要介意。"h現在就這樣放