dd Room"Empowered Ice Beam"Primeval Chill"Primeval Frost Spikes"Primeval Hail"Primeval Shiver Dance"Empowered Cruelty"Empowered Dragon Breath"Primeval Dragon Dance"Primeval Loom Over"Primeval Howl"Primeval Torment"Primeval Dream Dance"Primeval Moonglow"Primeval Puzzle Room"Test MoveIu;␀�+[[�"NThe user helps the target and makes it use its move right after the user."bThe user hurriedly and randomly uses a move among those known by other Pokémon in the party."TThe user maximizes its Attack stat in exchange for HP equal to half its max HP."WThe user passes its held item to the target when the target isn't holding an item."`The user endures attacks for two turns, then strikes back to cause double the damage taken."PThe user blocks the target's way with arms splayed wide to trap the target."[The user drops onto the target with its full body weight. It has a 30% chance to numb."eThe user attacks everything around it with the destructive power of a terrible, explosive sound."KThe user changes its type to become the same type as one of its moves."iThe user changes its type to make itself resistant to the type of the attack the opponent used last."hThe user approaches the target, then steals their item. Items stolen from wild Pokémon are stored."ZThe target is hit with rhythmically launched punches that have a 30% chance to dizzy."EA reckless, life-risking tackle. The user also takes 33% recoil."mThe user attacks the foe with an echoing voice. If this move is used every turn, it does greater damage."ZThe user compels the target to keep using only the move it last used for three turns."JAn attack move that cuts down the target's HP to equal the user's HP."aThe user endures any attack with at least 1 HP. It always fails if it is used in succession."jThe user dances to compel the target to mimic it, making the target's Ability the same as the user's."bThe user explodes to inflict damage on those around it. The user faints upon using this move."bThe user charges the target at blinding speed. This attack always goes before any other move."kDoubles its power if the user has a status condition. Ignores damage reduction from Burn or Frostbite."oAn attack that hits first and makes the target flinch. It only works the first turn the user is in battle."bThe user flails about aimlessly to attack. It becomes more powerful the less HP the user has."WEnables random critical hits for the user, and quadruples its critical hit chance."`The user draws attention to itself, making all targets take aim only at the user this turn."[The target is multi-hit two to five times with raking swipes. Can random critical hit."fThe user charges at the target using every bit of its power. The user must rest on the next turn."GThe user intimidates the target by staring at it to cause numbing."PThe user growls, scaring nearby foes. Their Attack is lowered by two steps."\The user stiffens all the muscles in its body to raise its Defense stat by three steps."dThe user sticks out its head and attacks by charging into the foe. It has a 50% chance to numb."`The user makes a soothing bell chime to heal the status problems of all the party Pokémon."NThe user assists an ally by boosting the power of its next attack by 50%."TThe user holds back when it attacks, and the target is left with at least 1 HP."hThe foe is attacked with a powerful beam. The user must rest on the next turn to regain its energy."jThe user bites hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It has a 40% to make the target flinch."SThe user lets loose a horribly echoing shout with the power to inflict damage."lThe user releases countless shots of light. Its type varies with the kind of Plate the user is holding."cThis move can be used only after the user has used all the other moves it knows in the battle."_The user leers at nearby foes with sharp eyes. Their Defense stat is reduced by two steps."`The user chants an incantation, preventing the foe from landing critical hits for 10 turns."hThe user tries to cut ahead of the foe to steal and use the foe's intended move with greater power."FThe target is slugged by a punch thrown with muscle-packed power."\The user waggles a finger and stimulates its brain into randomly using nearly any move.">The user restores its own HP by up to half of its max HP."qCloaking itself in high energy, the user slams into the target. This move's type depends on the held memory."^The user draws power to attack by using a held Berry. The Berry used determines its type."oAn attack that makes use of nature's power. Its effects and type vary depending on the user's environment."ZThe user intimidates all nearby foes, lowering their Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."]Numerous coins are hurled at the target to inflict damage. Money is earned after battle."IThe target is physically pounded with a long tail or a foreleg, etc."NIt enables the user to evade all attacks. It fails if used in succession."iThe user lunges at the target at a speed that makes it almost invisible. It is sure to strike first."sA spin attack that can also eliminate trapping and hazards afflicting your side. Also raises the user's Speed."QRestoring its own cells, the user restores its own HP by half of its max HP."XThe user recycles a held item that has been used in battle so it can be used again."PThe user reflects the target's type, making it the same type as the target.";The user rests to cure itself of any status condition."XAn ancient song appeals to the hearts of those listening. Switches Meloetta's form."hGets revenge for a fainted ally. If an ally fainted in the last turn, this attack's damage doubles."hThe user attacks the target by dancing very hard. The user's type determines the type of this move."HThe foe is forced to switch out to a random ally. Always goes last."fThe user attacks with a song. Others can join in the Round and make the attack do greater damage."_Hard, pointed, and sharp claws rake the target to inflict damage. Can random critical hit."UThe user's earsplitting screech reduces the target's Defense stat by four steps."iThe user blows up to inflict damage on all Pokémon in battle. The user faints upon using this move."MThe user's edges become sharper, raising its Attack stat by three steps."KThe user shouts with force at the target. This move always hits first."SThe user shoots a mysterious beam that changes the target's Ability to Simple."jIt enables the user to permanently learn the move last used by the foe. Once used, Sketch disappears."mThe user tucks in to raise its Defense by four steps in the first turn, then rams the foe on the second."KThe user slacks off, restoring its own HP by up to half of its max HP."UThe target is attacked with a slash of claws or blades. Can random critical hit."JWhile it is asleep, the user randomly uses one of the moves it knows."eThis attack inflicts double damage on a numbed foe. It also cures the target's numbing, however.";An attack that can be used only if the user is asleep."yThe power stored using the move Stockpile is released all at once in an attack. 150 base power per Stockpile charge."`The user shines a spotlight on the target so that only it will be attacked during the turn."nThe user charges up power and raises its Defense and Sp. Def by two steps. The move can be stacked twice."=Used only if the user has no PP. It also hurts the user."RThe user eats its held Berry, then raises Defense and Sp. Def by three steps."rThe user spends 25% HP to create a doll to protect it from move damage, additional effects, and status moves."dThe user chomps hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It cuts the target's HP to half."PThe user generates odd sound waves from its body. The target becomes dizzy."ZThe user consumes its Stockpile to heal for 50% max HP per charge. This can overheal."VStar-shaped rays are shot at the opposing team. Can't miss and skips protections."_A physical attack in which the user charges and slams into the target with its whole 