 stingers."qThe user makes a plea for survival, halving the damage their side takes from non-attack sources for 8 turns."\The user calls out its underlings to annoy the target with buzzing sounds, dizzying it."`The user prepares its weapons, raising Attack by six steps but lowering Speed by six steps."0The user rakes the target with sharp claws."xThe user bites, claws, and stings the target while rolling. It has a 20% chance each to poison, waterlog, or leech."^The target is plastered with irritating scales, damaging it and changing its type to Bug."vThe user sheds a huge volley of scales at the target. Lands without fail and lowers the user's Sp. Def and Speed."kIf the user is faster than the target, puts the target to sleep, then minimizes the user's Speed stat."fThe user stabs through the target using tremendous force. Lowers the user's Attack by four steps."lAvenging bugs everywhere, the user crushes the target. It has a 20% chance to lower their Defense stat."\The user stabs the target, injecting a painful chemical. It has a 30% chance to poison."[Halves attack damage taken this turn. Numbs any attackers. Fails if used successively."YThe user sucks the target's life. The user's HP is restored by 50% the damage dealt."\The user calls out its underlings to pummel the target. Skips and destroys protections."]The user summons bugs to terrorize the target, trapping and damaging it for three turns."YThe user amps itself up for performance, raising its Sp. Atk and Speed by two steps."mDisables the target's last used move for four turns, then reduces a relevant stat on them by four steps."oThe user attacks with bitter emotion. This lowers the target's Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps if in hail."WThe user causes a glitch in reality. This attack always results in a critical hit."`The user loses 25% of their max HP to curse the target, damaging their HP by 25% each turn."dThe user makes a dreadful bell noise, harming all near battlers with visions of impending doom."LThe target becomes trapped, and takes 50% more damage from all attacks."bThe user sings with deathly sounds to harm the target. It has a 20% chance to reduce Sp. Def."]The target is subjected to a violent and frightening prank. It has a 10% chance to numb."YThe user forces itself or the target to make a substitute by turning it into a doll."hThe user soothes the target, lowering its Speed by four steps. If in hail, they also become drowsy."vThe user channels its fallen allies to strike the target. This attack has 20 more power per fainted party member."PDisables the target's last used move for five turns, and cuts 5 PP from it."mSpectral hands reach from the ground to trip the target. The heavier the target, the greater the damage."�The user uses honey to fully restore their HP. However, this lures swarming insects, trapping and damaging the user for three turns."`Changes type based on machine haunted. 30% chance of extra effect based on machine haunted."DThe user switches out using a cruel illusion. Always goes last."pThe user opens its soul to unleash massive energy. This lowers the user's Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."bThe target becomes Cursed. Health lost from Curse becomes coins for you to earn after battle."iThe user summons apparitions that dance around hypnotically before they multi-hit two to five times."WThe user drains heat from the air around the target, afflicting it with frostbite."OThe user buries the target with somber force. Then, this move is disabled."cThe user absorbs the target's soul, lowering its Sp. Def and draining its life in the process."XThe user licks the target, numbing them, or cursing them if they're already numbed."gThe user unleashes its grudge, damaging the target and cutting 4 PP from the move last used by it."MThe user restores two thirds of its own HP. Then, this move is disabled."aThe user suffocates the target by sucking the air from their lungs. Can random critical hit."oThe user snips the target's connection to life in order to curse them, damaging their HP by 25% each turn."aThe user thins the air around the target, depriving them of oxygen. Can random critical hit."PThe target is pestered by a giant tongue. This has a 50% chance to numb it."iClad in souls, the user crashes into the target. The user takes 33% recoil, but can't faint from it."jThe user rips into the target's soul, dealing damage through their Sp. Def rather than their Defense."UThe user attacks while wailing. This has a 40% chance to make the target flinch."aThe user slashes with gusto, inspiring its allies to follow up by using Slash on the target."ZThe user uses gunpowder to rocket at its foe. It has a 30% chance to raise its Speed."RThe user becomes a pain train. It has a 10% chance to raise the user's Speed."ZA reckless charge that forces the user to switch out if it misses. Always goes first."vInflicts physical or special damage, whichever deals more. Then, raises Attack or Sp. Atk, whichever wasn't used."WConductive materials ensnare the target, trapping and damaging it for three turns."dThe user lays a hazard of sharp feathers around the foe. It hurts foes that switch into battle."The user dislodges a blast of thin projectiles. This attack always results in a critical hit, but applies Fracture to the user."sThe user uses explosive force to shoot shards of its own body at the target. The user loses 10% of its max HP."_The user curls its metal hair around the target, trapping and damaging it for three turns."dThe user headbutts the target with a metal head. It has a 20% chance to make the target flinch."�A large spike is shot at the target. If this causes the target to faint, a hazard layer of Spikes is set on the ground beneath them."LThe target is pierced with a sharp iron arrow. Can random critical hit."QThe target is pierced with a pointed metal javelin. Can random critical hit."`The user strikes the target while magnetizing it, trapping and damaging it for three turns."^The target is hit by a wave of magnetic energy. It has a 20% chance to lower their Speed."LProtects the user from attacks. Special attackers take 1/8th HP damage."fThe user attacks the target with a sword. If it faints, tons of money is earned after the battle."�The user creates a high quality area for eight turns in which super-effective deals 25% more, and not very effective deals 25% less."tThe user shoots a massive metal object at the target. The user must rest on the next turn to regain its energy."NThe user economizes half of its weight, healing based on the weight lost."WThe user launches a fist with extreme force. This attack is popular with children."jThe user crushes the target in its metallic vises, breaking any screens protecting the target's side."dThe user looses a flash of energy from its polished body. It has a 30% chance to lower Sp. Def."kProtects the user from damage this turn. It also lowers the Sp. Atk of special attackers by two steps."/The user hurls a metal ball at the target."\The user shoots shards of its own body at the target. The user loses 10% of its max HP."hThe user shreds off bits of its own body to launch at the target. The user loses 10% of its max HP."OThe user sprays mining waste at the target. It has a 30% chance to poison."\The user slashes at the target with a steel blade. Super effective versus Dragon-types."aThe user heals itself for half of their max HP, and extends the current weather by one turn."WThe user enters a protective stance, raising its Sp. Atk and Defense by two steps."ZThe user prepares its dual cannons. Until switch out, each special attack hits twice."[The user drags the target into the water with a heavy anchor. They become waterlogged."fWelds heavy steel onto the target, giving it the Steel type and reducing its Speed by four steps."hThe user ponders ancient wisdom, selecting three random status moves. You choose which one it uses."oSummons sunshine for five turns on the first turn, then overwhelms the foe with fiery light on the second."f