 attack damage taken this turn. Waterlogs any attackers. Fails if used successively."dThe user gains an instinctual knowledge of battle, raising its Attack and Sp. Def by two steps."UThe user crashes into the target with its quills. It leaves the target poisoned."oThe user propels a geyser of water at the target. This lowers the user's Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."UThe user crashes into the target like a tsunami. The user also takes 33% recoil."cThe user swims at the target at blinding speed. This attack always goes before any other move."HThe target is immersed in water. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."OThe user waterlogs the target, then welcomes in rainstorm for eight turns."WThe foe is pulled into a huge whirlpool, trapping and damaging it for three turns."wThe user opens a spring to blast the target, also forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."qAttacks with pressurized water. Deals 50% more damage if the user has been hurt by the foe in the same turn."`The user rams its sharp face right into the target. Lowers the user's Speed by three steps."VThe user crashes into the target on a ripping current. This waterlogs the target."kThe user rips the target, lowering their Defense by two steps. After attacking, the user switches out."SStrikes the target with harbor waters, then summons rainstorm for eight turns."�The user rests in a riverbed, restoring its HP by half of max, and forming an Aqua Ring around themselves, healing 10% HP per turn."oThe user attacks with a wave of murky water, which hits all near foes and lowers their Speed by two steps."bThe target is crushed in the user's shell or claws, trapping and damaging it for three turns."WThe user snaps like a fish at the target. This has a 40% chance to make it flinch."cThe user rams the target while splashing up a lot of water. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."ZThe user wields tidal power to grab at the target. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."`The user uses a jet of water l