r Steel-type move. Caps out at +4."KThe Pokémon and its allies' moves are twice as likely to be critical."@Leaves two hazard layers of Spikes after it self-destructs."sSpeed is raised each turn. Speed is reset when hit, but the attacker takes 1/8th HP damage for each step lost."?Can't be afflicted with any non-volatile status condition."AHas a 30% chance to dizzy targets when using physical moves."fPrevents stat steps from being lowered (except when self-inflicted). Immune to weather downsides."[Doubles critical hit chance for each Speed step up. All moves can random critical hit.">Sets a Light Screen for 4 turns upon entering the battle."SDuring eclipse, its moves can't miss and always activate their random effects."]Takes 50% less damage from Water-type moves. Raises Speed by four steps when hit by one."IImmune to Steel-type moves and restores 25% of max HP if hit by one.",Fly and Dive Bomb deal 50% more damage."+Can hold a second item by stealing it."FIf an attack lowers its HP to half or less, leeches the attacker."_Prevents half the self-damage from recoil. Powers up moves that have recoil damage by 20%."<Summons rainstorm for four turns when hit by an attack."LUpon entry, summons a Turbulent Sky on the Pokémon's side for 6 turns."cIgnores Abilities that would affect its moves. Its attacks can't be redirected to new targets."7Makes foes stressed and unable to use their items."MIn rainstorm, each of its hits is followed by an extra hit at 25% power."KPrevents its stats from being lowered by more than one step at a time."eIgnores Abilities that would affect its moves. Dizzies opponents that it hits below half health."mChanges the weather to Blood Moon, which heralds the Full Blood Moon. Lingers for 3 turns after leaving.";The Pokémon benefits twice as much from style points."TUpon entry, creates a Trick Room for four turns, inverting the effect of Speed."%Powers up Ice-type moves by 50%."TSpecial moves against the Pokémon have a 30% chance to frostbite the attacker."[Uses Rapid Spin after its first attack to clear hazards, raise Speed, and deal damage."#Boosts Sp. Atk by 30% in hail."uAt the end of each turn in sunshine, each Pokémon not immune to sunshine has their Defense and Sp. Def lowered."5Boosts the Pokémon's Attack by 30% in sunshine.":Summons eclipse for four turns when hit by an attack."'Powers up Water-type moves by 50%."=It avoids hazards and can't be knocked out with one hit."?The Pokémon's Speed is doubled while using kicking moves.",Boosts the power of blade moves by 30%."<During hail, boosts Speed and Grass-type damage by 50%.":Draws in attacks from enemies with below half health."8Deals 25% more move damage for each ally in battle."_At the end of each round, lowers other numbed Pokémon's Defense and Sp. Def by two steps."MBoosts damage by 20% if there is a weather. Immune to weather downsides.":Flinching moves always activate their random effects."\Becomes energy charged upon entry, doubling the power of its next Electric-type attack."dBy sacrificing a held item the Pokémon didn't start with, it can negate one attack against it."gBecomes energy charged when hit by an attack, doubling the power of its next Electric-type attack."HIts attacks have priority, deal 25% less damage and become special."?Between each turn there's another turn where no one moves."OFoes suffer 50% more move damage reduction from burn, frostbite, and numb."HUpon entry during eclipse, heals the lowest HP ally or self by 33%."GRestores its HP by 50% of the damage it deals to sleeping targets.":Takes half damage from Fighting- and Rock-type moves."APowers up Poison-type moves of itself and its allies by 50%."GHeals based on the damage other battlers take from being poisoned.""Traps the foe during eclipse.":Takes 30% less damage from Pokémon that are trapped."`Foes whose stats are lowered by the Pokémon keep those lowered stats even after switching.">The Pokémon's Speed is doubled while using recoil moves."jBoosts the power of sound moves by 30%. Sound moves ignore the target's modified Defense and Sp. Def."(Powers up Ground-type moves by 50%."-Powers up moves of the same type by 50%."5Takes half damage from Dark- and Bug-type moves."XBefore using a status move against a single foe, lowers their Defense by two steps."{Moves ignore Abilities that would affect its moves or activate after hitting the target, and immunities due to typing."KPrevents half the self-damage from recoil and Self-Destruct/Explosion."xIf an attacker would activate a random added effect on the Pokémon, that effect is placed on the attacker instead."NBlocks random added effects of attacks taken, and prevents critical hits."FMoves that use stats other than the default deal 50% more damage."<Takes 20% less damage from neutrally effective attacks."!The Pokémon is Mutant-type."BMakes the foe nervous and unable to eat Berries or Leftovers."nDeals 30% more damage to targets that have an item. After attacking a foe, destroys their clothing items."iAfter an attack reduces its HP to half or less, deals 1/4 of the attacker's HP back to the attacker."NImmune to Poison-type moves, and raises Attack and Sp. Atk if hit by one."HWhenever a foe's poison worsens, the Pokémon heals for 25% max HP."@Powers up Grass-type moves of itself and its allies by 50%."bHeals non-volatile status conditions and resets stat changes after knocking out any Pokémon."5Takes 40% less damage while using a status move."PAt the end of each turn, itself and each ally heals for 1/16th of their HP."KThe Pokémon's attacks are always critical if there is an active Room."Double Sp. Def in eclipse."CBoosts Speed by 50% in rainstorm. Can't miss during rainstorm."XImmune to weather downsides, and takes 20% less damage from attacks during weather."OTakes 50% less damage from not-very-effective or barely-effective attacks."VDraws in moves from foes with base power 100 or more. Takes 15% less move damage."7Uses Power Split upon entry or when hit by a move."LUpon entry, summons a Primal Forest on the Pokémon's side for 6 turns."WUpon entry, creates a Willful Room for four turns, reducing all hits by 30 damage.":During hail, immune to Fire- and Electric-type moves.";Restores HP based on damage taken by others from hail."ULays an electrical hazard around the opponent when its HP is lowered below half."EAfter knocking out any Pokémon, raises its Sp. Atk and Sp. Def."GThe random added effects of moves by all battlers always activate."7Ground-type moves deal 50% more damage in eclipse."CUses Dragon Dance if an attack lowers its HP to half or below."{Boosts the power of rampaging moves by 30%, and makes them physical or special based on which would be more effective."6The Pokémon starts as a very convincing Pikachu!":Transforms into the entire enemy team, except buffed!"8Heals for 1/4th of its HP at the end of every turn."!Attack and Speed are halved."�Switches out if its HP becomes half or less. The replacement Pokémon's ​​first hit must be a crit​​ and if it's Doduo or Dodrio, it will use Fly​​ immediately."�When hitting a target that has an ability with an offensive damage-modifying effect, the Pokémon ignores the conditions and triggers the effect."pTakes half damage from Dragon-, Fairy-, and Ghost-type attacks. Positive stat steps remain after switching."�When the Pokémon's level is 25 or higher, it transforms into a member of its family depending on the type of the move it is about to use."kBoosts both one offending and defending stat by one step according to the foe's defenses and offenses."\The power of its moves is increased by 20% every time it takes damage during Last Gasp.".Attacks switching opponents with Pursuit."OAdapts the move's type to ensure it is super-effective against the target."UAdapts the move's type to ensure it is truly super-effective against the target."ZAdapts the move's type to maximize effectiveness while accounting for the immunities."BAdapts the move's type to maximize damage against the target."@When the Pokémo